hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18601","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he ordered his companions to go out for battle, and he saw a man holding back, who said: I will pray the noon prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then greet him and bid him farewell so that he supplicates for me with a supplication that will go ahead for me on the Day of Resurrection. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, the man came forward greeting him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you know by how much your companions have preceded you? He said: Yes, they preceded me by their morning march of yesterday and today. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, they have indeed preceded you by as far as between the two easts and the two wests in virtue."
"18602","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18603","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the best of faith? He said: The best of faith is that you love for the sake of Allah, hate for the sake of Allah, and employ your tongue in the remembrance of Allah. He said: And what else, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And that you love for people what you love for yourself, hate for them what you hate for yourself, and that you speak good or remain silent."
"18604","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18605","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Shall I not inform you why Allah named Ibrahim His intimate friend, the one who fulfilled? Because he used to say every morning and evening: Glory be to Allah when you enter the evening and when you enter the morning, until he completed the verse."
"18606","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"18607","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: The verse of might belongs to Allah: Say: Praise be to Allah who has not taken a son, and has no partner in dominion, and has no protector out of weakness, and magnify Him greatly."
"18608","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The verse of might is: Say: Praise be to Allah who has not taken a son, and has no partner in dominion, and has no protector out of weakness, and magnify Him greatly."
"18609","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, al-Layth narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride these beasts while they are sound, and leave them at rest while they are sound."
"18610","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people standing by their beasts and mounts, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride them while they are sound, and dismount from them while they are sound, and do not take them as chairs for your conversations and gatherings, for many a ridden beast is better than its rider and more constant in remembrance of Allah than he."
"18611","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Sulayman, that Ismail ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri narrated to him, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever defends a believer against a hypocrite who backbites him, Allah will send an angel to protect his flesh on the Day of Resurrection from the fire of Hell; and whoever accuses a Muslim of something, seeking to disgrace him thereby, Allah will detain him on the bridge of Hell until he comes out of what he said."
"18612","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Khath'ami, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, who said: I went out on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on such-and-such campaign, and the people crowded the dwellings and cut off the road, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a caller who called out among the people: Whoever crowds a dwelling or cuts off a road has no striving in jihad."
"18613","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated, Baqiyya narrated, from al-Awza'i, from Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Qurra ibn Mujahid, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: We went out on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he sent a caller: Whoever crowds a dwelling or cuts off a road has no striving in jihad."
"18614","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the mu'adhdhin announcing the prayer, say as he says."
"18615","Al-Husayn ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the servants are servants to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, nor look at them. They said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: One who disowns his parents and turns away from them, one who disowns his child, and a man upon whom people bestowed a favor and he denied their favor and disowned them."
"18616","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My community will remain upon a good path as long as three things do not appear among them: as long as knowledge is not taken away from them, the child of sin does not multiply among them, and the saqqarun do not appear among them. It was said: O Prophet of Allah, what are the saqqarun? He said: A generation that will be at the end of time whose greeting among themselves is mutual cursing."
"18617","Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated; both said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, from Khayr ibn Nu'aym, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent out a detachment, and a woman came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband is going out with this detachment, and I used to pray with his prayer, fast with his fasting, and worship with his worship, so direct me to a deed by which I can catch up with his deed. So he said: Can you stand in prayer without pause, fast without breaking fast, and remember Allah without heedlessness? She said: O Messenger of Allah, can anyone bear that? So he said: Even if you were encumbered with that, by the One in whose Hand is my soul, you would not reach a tenth of that."
"18618","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My husband has gone out to fight in the path of Allah, and I used to follow his prayer when he prayed and his deeds; so inform me of a deed that will bring me to his deed until he returns? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Can you stand so as not to sit, remember so as not to flag, and fast so as not to break fast until he returns? She said: I cannot do this, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, even if you did, you would not reach a tenth of his deed until he returns."
"18619","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, and Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sits in his place of prayer after praying the morning prayer until he prays the forenoon prayer, saying nothing but good, his sins will be forgiven, even if they are more than the foam of the sea. And the wording is that of the hadith of Rishdin."
"18620","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever recites the beginning of Surat al-Kahf and its end, it will be a light for him from his feet to his head; and whoever recites it all, it will be a light for him from his feet to his head, from the earth to the sky."
"18621","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"18622","Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated, Rishdin narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah the Magnificent, a planting will be planted for him in Paradise; and whoever recites the Quran, masters it and acts upon what is in it, Allah will clothe his parents on the Day of Resurrection with a crown whose light is more excellent than this moon."
"18623","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym Dirar ibn Surad narrated, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever teaches knowledge, his is the reward of whoever acts upon it, and nothing is diminished from the reward of the doer."
"18624","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever honors his parents, glad tidings to him; Allah will increase his lifespan."
"18625","What al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated from Ma'qil ibn Yasar; Qatada from al-Hasan. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, from Shu'ba, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give the grandmother a sixth."
"18626","Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated, Mu'ammal ibn Ismail narrated, Hammad ibn Salama narrated, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no servant who is put in charge of a flock and dies while cheating it except that he will enter the Fire."
"18627","Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil. Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, both saying: Musaddad narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated, from al-Hasan, who said: While Ma'qil ibn Yasar was eating lunch a morsel fell from him, so he took it, removed whatever harm was in it, and ate it. It was said to him: May Allah set right the amir; these non-Arabs glance at one another because you eat the fallen morsel, while before you is this food. He said: I would not abandon for the sake of these non-Arabs what I heard; we used to be commanded that if the morsel of one of us fell, he should take it, remove whatever harm was on it, eat it, and not leave it for Satan."
"18628","Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Isbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Amir ibn Salih narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: We used to be commanded; then he mentioned the same."
"18629","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated, Attab ibn Harb narrated, al-Mada al-Khazzaz narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the morsel of one of you falls, let him remove whatever harm is on it, eat it, and not leave it for Satan."
"18630","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Hayjami narrated, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the morsel of one of you falls, let him remove whatever harm is on it and eat it."
"18631","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated, Attab ibn Harb narrated, from al-Mada al-Khazzaz, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, who said: Ma'qil ibn Yasar said: On the day of the Pledge of Ridwan I was holding up a branch of the tree over the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was pledging allegiance from the people; he did not pledge them unto death, he pledged them that they would not flee, and he used to shake hands with the women from under the garment."
"18632","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Ma'qil ibn Yasar fell ill and Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad came to visit him, so Ma'qil said to him: I shall narrate to you a hadith I never narrated to you; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no servant whom Allah puts in charge of a flock, then he dies while cheating it, except that Allah will forbid Paradise to him."
"18633","Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinna'i narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan who said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad entered upon Ma'qil ibn Yasar to visit him while we were with him, so Ma'qil said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any man whom Allah puts in charge of a flock, then he dies while cheating it, Allah will forbid Paradise to him."
"18634","Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Isbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Abu Isra'il al-Mula'i narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will never put a servant in charge of a flock who dies while cheating it except that Allah will forbid Paradise to him."
"18635","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated, Ismail ibn Ulaya narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18636","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i narrated to us, Uqba ibn Mukram narrated, Abdullah ibn Isa narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18637","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Uqba ibn Mukram narrated, Abdullah ibn Isa narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that he entered upon Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad to visit him, so Ma'qil said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The punishment of this community is the sword, their appointment is the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter."
"18638","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the grandmother the sixth."
"18639","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated, Abd al-A'la narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Umar said: Who knows the ruling of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the grandfather? So Ma'qil ibn Yasar said: He ruled a sixth for him."
"18640","Yusuf ibn Ya'qub the judge narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Amir ibn Salih narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Umar said: Who knows how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the grandfather? So Ma'qil ibn Yasar said to him: I do. He said to him: How much is his? He said: The sixth. He said: Who is with you? He said: I do not know. He said: You do not know."
"18641","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Isbahani narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, from Shu'ba, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the grandfather the sixth."
"18642","Al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Massisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated, and Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Yaman narrated; both said: Hushaym narrated, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning a grandfather who was among us, with the sixth."
"18643","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I take a goat to slaughter it and I pity it. He said: Even if you pity it, Allah will pity you."
"18644","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Salama ibn Shabib narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, concerning the word of Allah the Mighty and Majestic: So do not prevent them from marrying their husbands when they agree among themselves in a lawful manner. He said: Ma'qil ibn Yasar narrated to me that it was revealed concerning him. He said: I married a sister of mine to a man, and he divorced her, then left her until her waiting period ended, then he proposed to her. So I said: I married you, spread furnishings for you and honored you, then you divorced her; then you come to propose to her? No, by Allah, she will never return to you. He was a man of no fault, and she wanted to return to him, so Allah revealed this verse. So I said: Now I shall do it, O Messenger of Allah; and I married her to him."
"18645","Abbad ibn Rashid, from al-Hasan. Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Uqba ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated, and al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Isbahani narrated to us, Hilal ibn Bishr narrated, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated; both said: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated, from al-Hasan, Ma'qil ibn Yasar narrated, who said: I had a sister of mine who was sought in marriage and I kept her from people; then a cousin of mine came to me and I married her to him. They stayed together as long as Allah willed, then he divorced her with a divorce in which he had the right of return, and when her waiting period ended he came to propose to her along with the suitors. So I said to him: I kept her from people and preferred you with her and married her to you, then you divorced her; by Allah, I shall never marry her to you. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And when you divorce women and they reach their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands. So I expiated for my oath and married her to him."
"18646","Abu Attab, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil. Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Sallam ibn Miskin Abu Rawh narrated, Abu Attab narrated, from al-Hasan who said: Ziyad entered upon Ma'qil ibn Yasar while he was sick, visiting him, and he spoke to him, asked him and treated him gently. While they were thus, Ma'qil said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no ruler who takes charge of any affair of the Muslims and does not encompass those behind them with sincere counsel except that Allah will cast him into Hell upon his face on the day Allah gathers the first and the last."
"18647","Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Janub, from al-Hasan. Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Abu Ma'shar narrated, from Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Janub, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Medina is my place of migration and my resting place in the earth; it is a duty upon my community to honor my neighbors as long as they avoid the major sins. Whoever of them does not do that, Allah will give him to drink from the clay of khabal. We said: O Abu Yasar, what is the clay of khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"18648","Abdullah ibn Ahmad and Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Isbahani narrated to us, both saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Abu Damra Anas ibn Iyad narrated, from Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Janub, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslims are one hand against others; their blood is equal; no believer is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant."
"18649","Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan. Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, and Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Isbahani and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated; both said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, and Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated; both said: Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Jawari Abu al-Hawari narrated; both said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is put by Allah in charge of a flock, then dies while cheating it, Allah will forbid Paradise to him."
"18650","Awf ibn Abi Jamila, from al-Hasan. Bishr ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, both saying: Hawdha ibn Khalifa narrated, Awf narrated, from al-Hasan, who said: Ma'qil ibn Yasar fell ill with a grave illness, and Ibn Ziyad came to visit him. He said: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is put in charge of a flock and does not encompass them with sincere counsel will not find the fragrance of Paradise, though its fragrance is found from a distance of a hundred years. So Ibn Ziyad said: Why did you not narrate this to me before now? He said: Now, were it not for what I am in, I would not have narrated it to you."
"18651","Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn Hayyan al-Utaridi, from al-Hasan. Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, both saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated; both said: Abu al-Ashhab narrated, from al-Hasan, who said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad visited Ma'qil ibn Yasar in his illness in which he died, so Ma'qil said: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had I known I had life I would not have narrated it to you. I heard him say: There is no servant whom Allah puts in charge of a flock who dies the day he dies cheating his flock except that Allah will forbid Paradise to him. And the wording is that of Ali ibn al-Ja'd."
"18652","Al-Fadl ibn Dalham, from al-Hasan. Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Waki' narrated, from al-Fadl ibn Dalham, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that his sister was divorced by her husband, and he wanted to take her back but Ma'qil prevented her, so Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed concerning that: And when you divorce women and they reach their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands when they agree among themselves in kindness."
"18653","Mubarak ibn Fadala, from al-Hasan. Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated, from al-Hasan, that Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad came to Ma'qil ibn Yasar to visit him in his illness in which he died, and said: How do you find yourself? Ma'qil said: I do not see myself recovering from what is with me, and I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And what is it? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no one put in charge of a flock who dies the day he dies while cheating it, except that he will not find the fragrance of Paradise - or he said: among the people of the Fire. He said: Why did you not narrate this hadith to me before this day? He said: Were it not for what is with me, I would not have narrated it to you."
"18654","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar al-Muzani, that he married his sister to a man in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she stayed with him as long as she stayed, then he divorced her with one divorce and did not take her back until the waiting period ended. Then he desired her and she desired him, then he proposed to her along with the suitors. So he said to him: O base fellow, I honored you with her and married her to you, then you divorced her; by Allah, she will never return to you, the last thing upon you. So Allah knew his need for her and her need for him, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And when you divorce women and they reach their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands when they agree among themselves in kindness, to the end of the verse. When Ma'qil heard it, he said: Hearing and obedience to my Lord. Then he called him and said: I marry you and honor you."
"18655","Al-Rabi' ibn Subayh, from al-Hasan. Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated, from al-Hasan, that Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad entered upon Ma'qil ibn Yasar while he was gravely ill, and he said: I shall narrate to you a hadith; were it not for the condition I am in, I would not have narrated it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is put by Allah in charge of a flock and does not encompass those behind it with sincere counsel is among the people of the Fire. He said: Was this not before this?"
"18656","Zayd Abu al-Mu'alla, from al-Hasan. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated; both said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, who said: I heard Zayd Abu al-Mu'alla narrating, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever enters into any of the prices of the believers to raise it against them, it is due upon Allah to punish him in the mightiest part of Hell."
"18657","Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn A'yan narrated to me, from Abu al-Mu'alla, who said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever enters into anything of the prices of the Muslims to raise it against them, then upon Allah is to hurl him into a mighty part of the Fire."
"18658","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated, Zayd ibn Abi Layla Abu al-Mu'alla narrated, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil - meaning ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18659","Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Hasan. Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn al-Isbahani narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"18660","Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated, Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated, who said: A group of the people of Basra - among them al-Hasan - testified before me concerning Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man while he was being cupped while fasting, and said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"18661","Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated, Waki' narrated, from al-Fadl ibn Dalham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the woman who joins hair and the woman for whom it is joined."
"18662","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated, Waki' narrated, from al-Fadl ibn Dalham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman who has it joined."
"18663","Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shaddad ibn Sa'id al-Rasibi narrated, who said: I heard Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir say: I heard Ma'qil ibn Yasar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That an iron spike be driven into the head of one of you is better for him than that he touch a woman not lawful to him."
"18664","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated, who said: My father informed me, Shaddad ibn Sa'id narrated, from Abu al-Ala, Ma'qil ibn Yasar narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That a man be stabbed in the head with an iron spike is better for him than that he touch a woman not lawful to him."
"18665","Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Yusuf the judge narrated to us, both saying: Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship in turmoil is like migration to me."
"18666","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deed in turmoil is like migration to me."
"18667","Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, Bundar narrated, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Silafi narrated, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship in turmoil is like migration to me."
"18668","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship in turmoil is like migration to me."
"18669","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated; both said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Maslama ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafi narrated, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship in trial is like migration to me."
"18670","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir ibn bint Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Surur ibn al-Mughira narrated, from Sulayman al-Thaqafi, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship in trial is like migration to me."
"18671","Abu Ya'la Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Shadhan narrated to us, my father narrated, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated, from al-A'mash, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship in turmoil - or in trial - is like migration to me."
"18672","Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Mazini, Ibrahim ibn Na'ila and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, who said: Muhammad ibn Ubayy al-Muqaddami narrated, Aghlab ibn Tamim narrated, from Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of my community my intercession will not reach: an unjust treacherous ruler, and one extreme in religion; he testifies against them then disowns them."
"18673","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Mani' informed me, Mu'awiya ibn Qurra narrated to me, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men of my community my intercession will not reach: an unjust treacherous ruler, and another extreme in religion, apostatizing from it."
"18674","Abdan ibn Ahmad and Abu Ubayda Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us, both saying: Dawud ibn Bakr al-Tustari narrated, Hibban ibn Aghlab ibn Tamim narrated, from his father, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a key, and the key of the heavens is the saying: There is no god but Allah."
"18675","Abdan ibn Ahmad and Abu Ubayda Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, both saying: Dawud ibn Bakr al-Tustari narrated, Hibban ibn Aghlab ibn Tamim narrated, from his father, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever people among whom the call to prayer is made in the morning, they are in the protection of Allah until evening; and whatever people upon whom the call to prayer is made in the evening, they are in the protection of Allah until morning."
"18676","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Sallam ibn Sulaym al-Tawil narrated, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cupping on Tuesday, the seventeenth of the month, is a cure for a year's ailment."
"18677","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated; both said: Sallam al-Tawil narrated, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord the Exalted said: Son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship, I shall fill your heart with riches and fill your hands with provision; son of Adam, do not keep away from Me, lest I fill your heart with poverty and fill your hands with occupation."
"18678","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, Sallam al-Tawil narrated, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not listen to anything as He listens to the call of the mu'adhdhins and the beautiful voice with the Quran."
"18679","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'ara narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Samina narrated; all said: Al-Khalil ibn Ahmad narrated - and al-Abbas al-Anbari said: Al-Khalil ibn Ahmad ibn Bashir ibn al-Mustanir al-Sulami narrated to me - al-Mustanir ibn Akhdar ibn Mu'awiya ibn Qurra narrated, from his father, who said: I was with Ma'qil ibn Yasar on one of the roads; we passed by something harmful and he removed it - or moved it - from the road. I saw the like of it, so I took it and moved it aside. He took my hand and said: O son of my brother, what moved you to do what you did? I said: O uncle, I saw you do something, so I did the like. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever removes harm from the road of the Muslims, a good deed will be written for him; and whoever has a good deed accepted from him will enter Paradise. And the wording is that of the hadith of al-Abbas al-Anbari."
"18680","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated, al-Mufaddal ibn Ubaydullah narrated, Umar ibn Amir narrated, from Dawud ibn Yasar, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, the people took donkeys and seized them until the pots boiled. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and it was said: The people's donkeys have been slaughtered. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys. So a man overturned the vessel with the tip of his bow and the pole of his tent."
"18681","Abu Zur'a al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, al-Muthanna ibn Awf narrated, Abu Abdullah al-Jasri narrated, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar that he asked him about drink, so he said: We were in Medina, and it had abundant dates, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-fadikh."
"18682","Al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, Jami' ibn Matar narrated, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, that Ma'qil ibn Yasar said: Wine was forbidden while we were drinking al-fadikh, so I poured it out and said: This is the last covenant with wine."
"18683","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Shayba ibn Abi Bakr narrated, Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Nahhas narrated, Khalid ibn Ajlan narrated, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no man who takes charge of people then does not guard them as he guards himself and his family except that Allah will admit him into the fire of Hell."
"18684","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Dinar, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba entered wearing khuffs; he was the first I saw wearing khuffs in Islam, al-Mughira. The people began touching them and saying: What is this? They said: These are khuffs. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will have many khuffs. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us for ablution for prayer? He said: You wipe over them or perform ablution over them."
"18685","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ismail ibn Hud narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, al-Mustalim ibn Sa'id informed us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that a man mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he had found a woman of beauty and status, except that she does not bear children, so he forbade him from her. Then he returned, and he forbade him from her, and said: Marry the loving fertile, for I boast of you."
"18686","Abu Zur'a al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ata ibn Ajlan, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that Uthman ibn Affan used to suffer severely from madhy, so he sent a man to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is madhy; every stallion emits madhy. Wash it with water, perform ablution and pray."
"18687","Abu Abi Uthman, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated, from Abu Uthman - not al-Nahdi - from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Recite it over your dead, meaning Ya Sin."
"18688","Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from his father, from a man, from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Baqara is the hump of the Quran and its peak; with every verse of it eighty angels descended. And Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer, was taken from beneath the Throne and joined with it - or joined - with Surat al-Baqara. And Ya Sin is the heart of the Quran; no man recites it seeking Allah and the Hereafter except that Allah will forgive him. And recite it over your dead."
"18689","Ubaydullah ibn Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Imran al-Qattan narrated, from Ubaydullah ibn Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Act upon the Book of Allah and do not belie anything of it; what is obscure to you, ask the people of knowledge about it and they will inform you. And believe in the Torah and the Gospel, for in it is the explanation, and it is an intercessor, a prosecutor believed."
"18690","The cousin of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from Ma'qil. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir narrated, from his father, from the cousin of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: Ziyad entered upon him and said: Allah used to benefit us through knowledge by sitting with you, and you used to narrate to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Ma'qil said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes charge of any affair of the Muslims and does not encompass them with counsel as he encompasses his household, let him take his seat in the Fire. He said: I never heard this from you before today. He said: I would not have narrated it to you except while in this condition of mine. He said: So Ziyad went out dragging his garment."
"18691","The daughter of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from her father. Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Marwan ibn Mu'awiya narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, Ismail al-Awdi informed me, who said: I was in the house of Ma'qil ibn Yasar in Basra, and his daughter narrated to me that her father grew gravely ill, and that reached Ziyad. He came until he sought permission at the door, and I sat with my father. Ziyad entered and recognized death in my father's face, and said: O Ma'qil, will you not leave us provision from you? Allah used to benefit us with things we heard from you. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no governor of a community, large or small, who does not act justly among them except that Allah will cast him upon his face in the Fire. He lowered his head a while, then bowed it, then raised his head and said: O Ma'qil, is it something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or from beyond beyond? He said: Rather I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18692","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated; both said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Ismail al-Awdi, the daughter of Ma'qil ibn Yasar informed me, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same report."
"18693","Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Isbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from a man of Muzayna, from the daughter of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"18694","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Ismail al-Kindi, who said: I came to Basra and stayed in the house of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, and his daughter Hind narrated to me, saying: When my father grew gravely ill, that reached Ziyad ibn Abi Sufyan, and he came to visit him. He said: Allah used to benefit us with your hadith, so narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no governor employed over a community of my community, small or large, who does not act justly among them except that Allah will cast him upon his face in the Fire."
"18695","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Isbahani narrated, Abu Usama narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, Ismail al-Azraq narrated to me, from the daughter of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from her father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no governor who takes charge of a community, small or large, then does not act justly among them except that Allah will cast him into the Fire."
"18696","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Isra'il narrated, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim, the daughter of Ma'qil ibn Yasar narrated to me, saying: My father fell ill with the illness in which he died, and Ziyad came to visit him. He said: Admit him alone. So they admitted him. When he entered upon him, he said: Your hadith used to benefit us, so narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no governor who works over a community of my community, small or large, who does not act justly among them except that Allah will cast him upon his face in the Fire. That displeased him, so he said: Is it something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or heard from his companions? He said: Rather something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18697","Abu al-Rabab, freedman of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from Ma'qil. Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, and Abu Khalifa narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated; all said: Al-Hakam ibn Tahman Abu Azza al-Dabbagh narrated, Abu al-Rabab, freedman of Ma'qil ibn Yasar, narrated, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we came upon a place with garlic, and people took some of it, then came to the prayer place. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found its smell and said: Whoever eats of this plant, let him not approach our prayer place. And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walid."
"18698","Abu Abdullah al-Jasri, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan narrated, al-Muthanna ibn Awf narrated, Abu Abdullah al-Jasri narrated, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that he asked him about drink. He said: We were in Medina, and it had abundant dates, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us al-fadikh."
"18699","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Anbari narrated, and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Musa ibn Hibban al-Basri narrated; both said: Salm ibn Qutayba narrated, from Imran al-Qattan, from Qatada, from Abu Abdullah al-Jasri, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Majestic and Mighty disliked for you gossip, much questioning, and wasting wealth."
"18700","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated, Sa'id ibn al-Fadl al-Qurashi narrated, Sa'id ibn Iyas al-Jurayri narrated, from Abu Abdullah al-Anazi, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a slave to free him, let him not stipulate emancipation for its people, for his contract is a release from bondage."
"18701","Abu al-Malih ibn Usama al-Hudhali, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, and Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Bundar narrated; both said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no commander put in charge of a flock who does not encompass it and give sincere counsel to them except that he will not enter Paradise with them."
"18702","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Uqba ibn Mukram narrated, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Humayd al-Hudhali narrated, Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali narrated, Ma'qil ibn Yasar narrated to me who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Act upon the Quran, permit its lawful, forbid its unlawful, follow it, and do not disbelieve in anything of it; what is obscure to you, refer it to Allah or to the commander after me so that they inform you. And believe in the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and what the prophets were given from their Lord. Let the Quran intercede for you and what is in it of explanation, for it is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted, a prosecutor believed. Every verse of it has a light until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed I was given Surat al-Baqara from the remembrance, I was given Ta Ha and al-Tur from the tablets of Musa, I was given the Opening of the Book and the endings of al-Baqara from a treasure beneath the Throne, and I was given al-Mufassal as an extra."
"18703","Abdullah ibn Najiya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated, Bakr ibn Ibrahim narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Humayd narrated, from Abu al-Malih, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: We performed hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he found Aisha taking off her clothes. He said to her: What is with you? She said: I was told that you have exited ihram and released your family. He said: Yes, whoever has no sacrificial animal with him; as for us, we have not exited, with us are camels until we reach Arafat."
"18704","Himyari ibn Bashir, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated, from Qatada, from Himyari ibn Bashir, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah disliked for you three: disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding."
"18705","Iyad Abu Khalid al-Bajali, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Shu'ba, Iyad Abu Khalid narrated to me, who said: There was an oath between two neighbors of mine, and the oath fell upon one of them. So I heard Ma'qil ibn Yasar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath by which he cuts off the wealth of his brother will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"18706","529 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from 'Iyad Abu Khalid, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as it (the previous report)."
"18707","Al-Hakam al-A'raj, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. 530 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Khalid narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from al-Hakam al-A'raj, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah while I was lifting the branch of the tree away from his face; we pledged to him not to flee, and we did not pledge to him unto death. So they said to him: How many were you? He said: One thousand four hundred."
"18708","531 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated; both said: 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated, from al-Hakam ibn 'Abdillah, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I was holding up the branches of the tree over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the people pledged not to flee, and on that day they were one thousand four hundred."
"18709","532 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinna'i narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from al-Hakam ibn 'Abdillah ibn al-A'raj, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: You have indeed seen me on the day of the Tree while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taking the pledge from the people, and I was holding a branch of its branches above his head; we did not pledge to him unto death, but we pledged to him not to flee."
"18710","Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali, from Ma'qil. 533 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated, (ha) and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated; both said: Sawadah ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no shepherd who betrays his flock except that he is in the Fire."
"18711","534 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i narrated to us, 'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated, Sawadah ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated, from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as it."
"18712","Abu Taliq, from Ma'qil. 535 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Nasr ibn Tarif narrated, from Sulayman al-Taymi, Taliq narrated to me, from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever separates (a child from its mother / kin) is not of us. Asad said: He separates between the child and its mother and between brothers."
"18713","'Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Ma'qil. 536 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from his father, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar al-Muzani, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was brought an inheritance case involving a grandfather, and he gave him a third or a sixth."
"18714","Nafi' ibn Abi Nafi', from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. 537 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Asadi narrated, Khalid ibn Tahman narrated, from Nafi' ibn Abi Nafi', from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever says in the morning three times: I seek refuge in Allah, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from the accursed Satan, and recites three times the end of Surat al-Hashr, Allah appoints over him seventy thousand angels who invoke blessings upon him until evening; if he dies on that day he dies a martyr; and if he says it in the evening it is the same."
"18715","538 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Asadi narrated, Khalid ibn Tahman narrated, from Nafi' ibn Abi Nafi', from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and he said to me: Would you like Fatimah - meaning his daughter? I said: Yes. So he stood leaning on me and said: Yet another than you shall bear the burden, and the reward shall be yours. It was as if there was nothing upon me until we entered upon Fatimah, and he said to her: How do you find yourself? She said: By Allah, my grief has intensified, my poverty has intensified, and my illness has prolonged. He said: Are you not pleased that I married you to the foremost of my ummah in submission (to Islam), the most knowledgeable of them, and the most forbearing of them in forbearance?"
"18716","539 - Abu 'Arubah narrated to us, Abu al-Mu'afa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Nufay' ibn al-Harith, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to judge among my people, so I said: I am not skilled. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is with the judge so long as he does not deliberately deviate."
"18717","540 - 'Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Hamzah ibn 'Umayr informed, Ayyub ibn Ibrahim Abu Yahya al-Mu'allim narrated, from Ibrahim al-Sa'igh, from Abu Khalid ibn Khalid al-Dabbi, from Abu Dawud, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to judge among my people, so I said: I am not skilled at judging. He said: Judge among them, for Allah Almighty is with the judge so long as he does not deliberately deviate."
"18718","An unnamed man, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar. 541 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from his father, a man narrated to me, from his father, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Baqarah is the hump of the Qur'an and its peak; with every verse of it eighty angels descended; and (Allah! There is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer) was taken out from beneath the Throne and joined to Surat al-Baqarah; and Ya-Sin is the heart of the Qur'an: no man recites it seeking Allah and the Last Day except that Allah forgives him; recite it over your dead."
"18719","Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'i. 542 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: She is entitled to the dowry of her womenfolk, with neither undervaluation nor excess, and upon her is the waiting period, and to her is the inheritance. Then Abu Sinan al-Ashja'i stood up among a group of Ashja', and they testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged so in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq al-Ashja'i."
"18720","543 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, who said: 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud was approached and asked about a man who married a woman without fixing a dowry for her and without consummating with her until he died; they kept coming back to him, then he said: I shall give my opinion in it; if it is correct it is from Allah, and if it is wrong it is from me: I hold that she gets the dowry of a woman of her womenfolk - with neither undervaluation nor excess - and upon her is the waiting period, and to her is the inheritance. Then Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'i stood and said: I bear witness that you have judged in it as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq, a woman of Banu Ruwas, a clan of Banu 'Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah. And Sufyan holds by it."
"18721","544 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, that Ibn Mas'ud was approached concerning a man who died leaving his wife without having consummated with her and without fixing a dowry for her; they kept coming to him about it for a month while he said nothing about it, then he said: I shall give my opinion in it; if it is wrong it is from myself, and if it is correct it is from Allah. I say: To her is the dowry of her womenfolk, upon her is the waiting period, and to her is the inheritance. Then Ma'qil ibn Yasar al-Ashja'i stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq as you have judged. And Ibn Mas'ud rejoiced."
"18722","545 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, who said: 'Abdullah was approached concerning a man who left his wife without having consummated with her; they kept coming to him about it for a month while he gave no judgment in it, then he said: I shall give my opinion in it; if it is wrong it is from myself, and if it is correct it is from Allah: The like of the dowry of her womenfolk, upon her is the waiting period, and to her is the inheritance. Then Abu Sinan al-Ashja'i stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged so in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq. And 'Abdullah rejoiced at that."
"18723","546 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Abu 'Ubaydah 'Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-'Askari narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated, al-Muharibi narrated, Yazid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dalani narrated, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah, concerning a man who married a woman then died leaving her without consummating with her and without fixing anything for her; he said: To her is the full dowry, upon her is the waiting period, and to her is the inheritance. Then Ma'qil ibn Sinan said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge so in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq."
"18724","547 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated, saying: A group of the people of Basrah testified in my presence - among them al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan - from Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was being cupped on the eighteenth night past of Ramadan, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"18725","548 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Musa ibn Ya'qub, (ha) and Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-'Attar al-Makki and Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Ma'n ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Huwayrith, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: Ma'qil ibn Sinan came to me and informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar, Aslam, Juhaynah and Muzaynah are the clients of Allah Almighty and His Messenger."
"18726","Ma'qil ibn Abi Ma'qil al-Asadi. 549 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-San'ani narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Yahya ibn 'Amr informed me, from Abu 'Ammar al-Ansari, that Abu Zayd, the freedman of Tha'labah, informed him, that Ma'qil ibn Abi Ma'qil al-Asadi, of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade facing the two qiblas with stool or urine."
"18727","550 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-'Attar informed, from 'Amr ibn Yahya, from Abu Zayd, the freedman of Tha'labah, from Ma'qil ibn Abi Ma'qil al-Asadi, that he narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade facing the two qiblas with stool or urine."
"18728","551 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abi Isma'il, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Ma'qil ibn Abi Ma'qil, that his mother Zaynab came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Ma'qil had promised me that he would not perform Hajj except with me, then he performed Hajj on his mount and I was unable; so I asked him for the date-harvest of his palm trees and he said: It is the provision of my dependents; and I asked him for a young camel of his and he said: It is in the path of Allah, I shall not give it to you. He said: O Abu Ma'qil, what does Umm Ma'qil say? He said: She has spoken the truth. He said: Give her your young camel, for Hajj is the path of Allah. So he gave her his young camel. She said: I am a woman who has grown sick and old, and I fear I shall not live to reach Hajj until I die; is there anything that suffices in place of Hajj? He said: Yes, an 'Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj. So she performed 'Umrah in Ramadan."
"18729","Those named Miqdad. Miqdad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Aswad, a Badri; and it is said: Abu 'Amr, ally of Banu Zuhrah; and there is disagreement over his lineage: an Emigrant or a Badri. 552 - Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr."
"18730","553 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, saying: al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad ibn 'Amr."
"18731","The lineage of al-Miqdad, and mention of his description, age and death. 554 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated, Ziyad ibn 'Abdillah al-Bakka'i narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr ibn Tha'labah ibn Rabi'ah ibn Thumamah ibn Matrud ibn 'Amr ibn Sa'd ibn Zuhayr ibn Thawr ibn Tha'labah ibn Malik ibn Hazl ibn Qabis ibn Duraym ibn al-Qayn ibn Ahwad ibn Bahra' ibn 'Amr ibn al-Haf ibn Quda'ah; he was attributed to al-Aswad ibn 'Abd Yaghuth ibn Wahb ibn 'Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah because he adopted him and allied with him. He was dark-skinned, big-bellied, dyed his beard yellow, aquiline with a long nose. He died in Medina at seventy years of age, and 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with them both) prayed over him."
"18732","555 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ghundar narrated, from Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: I saw al-Miqdad, and he was bulky."
"18733","556 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, from Hariz ibn 'Uthman, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, Abu Rashid al-Hubrani narrated to me, saying: I saw al-Miqdad, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sitting on a chest of the money-changers' chests at Hims, overhanging it due to his size, intending to go on campaign. I said: Allah has indeed excused you. He said: The chapter of expeditions has refused us: (March forth, light and heavy)."
"18734","557 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, who said: al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad was of Kindah."
"18735","558 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shimasah, from Sufyan ibn Suhbanah al-Mahri, who said: I was the companion of al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad in the pre-Islamic period; he was a man of Bahra' who incurred blood-guilt among them, so he fled to Kindah and allied with them, then he incurred blood-guilt among them and fled to Mecca and allied with al-Aswad ibn 'Abd Yaghuth."
"18736","559 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Maslamah ibn 'Alqamah narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, that al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad borrowed seven thousand from 'Uthman ibn 'Affan; when he demanded it from him he said: It is only four thousand. So he disputed with him before 'Umar; 'Uthman said: I lent him seven thousand, and al-Miqdad said: Will you swear that it is seven thousand? He said: You have been fair. But he refused to swear, so he said: Take what he gives you. He said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, it is only seven thousand? He said: What prevents you from swearing: that this is night and this is day?"
"18737","560 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, saying: al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad died at al-Jurf, and men carried him to Medina on their necks in the year thirty-three; 'Uthman ibn 'Affan prayed over him. His kunyah was Abu Ma'bad, and his age was about seventy."
"18738","What al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad transmitted. 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad. 561 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, Abu Ya'la al-Thawri narrated, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, that 'Ali said: I was shy to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhiy (prostatic fluid), as his daughter was under me (in marriage); so I commanded al-Miqdad and he asked him, and he said: In it is ablution."
"18739","562 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ata', from 'A'ish ibn Anas, who said: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me about a man who fondles his wife and talks to her so that he emits madhiy; were it not that I am shy before him, and that his daughter is under me, I would have asked him. So al-Miqdad asked him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him wash his private part, then let him perform ablution, then let him sprinkle (water on) his garment."
"18740","563 - Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from 'Urwah, that 'Ali said: I said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for were it not that his daughter is under me I would have asked him, about one of us when he draws near his wife and emits madhiy without controlling it and without touching her? So al-Miqdad asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you emits madhiy without touching her, let him wash his private part and his testicles."
"18741","564 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-'Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from al-Miqdad, who said: 'Ali said to me: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who fondles his wife so that madhiy comes out of him? I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who fondles his wife so that madhiy comes out of him? He said: He washes his private part and performs his ablution for prayer."
"18742","Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Miqdad. 565 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Awn al-Wasiti narrated, Khalid ibn 'Abdillah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: A man came and praised 'Uthman, so al-Miqdad stood throwing dust in his face. 'Uthman said to him: What is wrong with you? He said: As for me, I shall not leave anything I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."
"18743","566 - 'Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, Bakr ibn Khunays narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Miqdad, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."
"18744","Al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad al-Fihri, from al-Miqdad. 567 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abu Hatim Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Baghdadi narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, who said: al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad said: When we emigrated to Medina, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportioned us ten by ten; I was among the ten who were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We had a ewe whose milk we drank among us. One night he was late for us, though we had set aside his share for him. I got up to it while hungry and drank it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came - and I had not slept - and went to the vessel in which we used to put the milk; he looked and found nothing in it. I leapt up and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not slaughter it for you? He said: No."
"18745","Tariq ibn Shihab al-Ahmasi, from al-Miqdad. 568 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, my father narrated to me, al-A'mash narrated to me, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had divided us ten to a house, ten to a house; I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we had a ewe whose milk was our sustenance."
"18746","569 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated, from al-A'mash, from Sulayman ibn Maysarah, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from al-Miqdad, who said: When we settled in Medina, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grouped us ten by ten in each house; I was among the ten with whom the Prophet was. We had only a ewe whose milk we shared; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was late for us we would drink and keep the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) share for him. One night he was late for us - and we had slept - and al-Miqdad said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been long; I do not think he will come tonight; perhaps someone invited him. So I drank it. When the night had passed he came and entered; when he entered he greeted without raising (his voice), then stood toward the cup; when he saw nothing he fell silent, then said: O Allah, feed whoever feeds us tonight. I leapt up, took the knife and brought it to him; he wiped her udder and something came out, then he drank, then he slept."
"18747","Sa'id ibn al-'As, from al-Miqdad. 570 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Sa'id ibn al-'As, who said: A delegation of the people of Iraq sent to 'Uthman and began praising him, so al-Miqdad began throwing dust in their faces, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."
"18748","Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from al-Miqdad. 571 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abbad al-Makki narrated to me, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, who said: I accompanied Talhah ibn 'Ubaydillah and al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, and I never heard any of them narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except that I heard Talhah narrate about the day of Uhud."
"18749","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Miqdad. 572 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, (ha) and 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, both said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated; both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Thabit al-Bunani, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr, who said: I arrived in Medina with two companions of mine; we began presenting ourselves to people but no one hosted us, so we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, severe hunger has struck us; we presented ourselves to people but no one hosted us. He took us to his house, where he had four goats, and said: O Miqdad, milk them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportioned for each person among us a share, and I used to do that; I set aside the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) share, but he was late for us, so I lay down on my bed. My soul said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has gone to a household of the Ansar and eaten and drunk with them; what if you drank this drink? My soul kept at me until I drank it. When it settled in my belly, I was seized by what is past and what is to come; my soul said to me: He will come now thirsty and find nothing. So I lay down and covered myself with the garment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and greeted with a greeting that the wakeful could hear but would not wake the sleeper, then went to the vessel, uncovered it and saw nothing in it, and said: O Allah, feed whoever feeds me and give drink to whoever gives me drink. I seized his supplication, rose, took the cleaver and approached the sheep; I looked for which of them was fattest to slaughter it. I approached one, felt it, and lo, it was full-uddered; I looked at another, and lo, it was full-uddered; I looked at another, and lo, it was full-uddered; I looked at all of them and lo, they were all full-uddered. So I milked into it and said: Drink. He said: The news, O Miqdad. I said: Drink, then the news. He said: Some of your misdeed, O Miqdad. He drank, then said: Drink. I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah. He drank until he was satiated, then I took from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and drank, then I informed him of the news. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a blessing that descended from heaven; why did you not inform me so that I could give your two companions to drink? I said: Since I and you have had (our share), I do not care who missed out."
"18750","573 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu Talib 'Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Thabit al-Bunani, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Miqdad, who said: I came with two companions of mine, our hearing and sight nearly gone from hardship, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he went to his family, and there were goats therein, and he said: Set right. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"18751","Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from al-Miqdad. 574 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, who said: A man came praising an agent of 'Uthman ibn 'Affan in the presence of al-Miqdad, so al-Miqdad threw dust in his face, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces."
"18752","Hammam ibn al-Harith, from al-Miqdad. 575 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hadrami and 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, both said: 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, 'Ubaydullah al-Ashja'i narrated, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us, when we see the flatterers, to throw dust in their faces."
"18753","576 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."
"18754","577 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (ha) and 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated; both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from al-Miqdad, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."
"18755","578 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Jabir al-Awdi narrated, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Mughirah, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from al-Miqdad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces."
"18756","Abu Ma'mar 'Abdullah ibn Sakhbarah, from al-Miqdad. 579 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."
"18757","580 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, both said: 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, al-Walid ibn 'Uqbah narrated, Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ma'mar al-Azdi, who said: A man stood praising an emir of the emirs, so al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad stood and threw dust in his face, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."
"18758","Yazid ibn Sharik al-Taymi, from al-Miqdad. 581 - 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yunus al-Lu'lu'i narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, who said: A man entered upon 'Uthman while al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad al-Kindi was with him; the man praised 'Uthman to his face, and al-Miqdad kept throwing dust at the man until 'Uthman shielded himself with a cloak of silk-brocade. Then al-Miqdad said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you hear the flatterers, throw dust in their faces."
"18759","'Abdullah al-Bahiyy, freedman of Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miqdad. 582 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated, (ha) and 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated; both said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Wa'il ibn Dawud, (ha) and al-Miqdad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, Wa'il ibn Dawud narrated, 'Abdullah al-Bahiyy, freedman of Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr, narrated: A company stopped at 'Uthman and praised him and extolled him - and al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad was there - so he took a handful of earth and threw dust in their faces, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces."
"18760","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from al-Miqdad. 583 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I and a man of the polytheists exchange two blows and he cuts off my hands, then when I raise (my hand) to him to strike him he says: There is no god but Allah - shall I kill him or leave him? He said: Rather leave him. I said: Even if he cut off my hands? He said: Even if he did. I repeated to him two or three times, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you kill him after he says: There is no god but Allah, then you are like him before he said it, and he is like you if you kill him."
"18761","584 - Abu Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani' al-Rusafi narrated, my grandfather narrated, from al-Zuhri, 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Junda'i narrated, that 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him, from al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - a man of Kindah, ally of Banu Zuhrah - who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the polytheists and I and he exchange two blows, and he severs one of my hands, then I strike him, then I gain power to kill him, and he says when I am about to raise my weapon to him: There is no god but Allah - shall I kill him or leave him? He said: Rather leave him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands? He said: Even if he did. I repeated to him, and he said: If you kill him after he says: There is no god but Allah, then you are in his position before he said it, and he is in your position before you kill him."
"18762","585 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated, al-Layth informed, (ha) and Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from al-Miqdad, that he informed him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the disbelievers and he fights me and strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: I have submitted to Allah - shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he says it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not kill him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off my hand, then said that after cutting it - shall I kill him? He said: Do not kill him; for he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he says the word he said."
"18763","586 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih al-Misri narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Ma'bad narrated, Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated, from Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar, who said: al-Miqdad said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Prophet of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the disbelievers and he fights me and strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: I have submitted to Allah - shall I kill him after he says it, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Do not kill him. He said: He cut off my hand, then said that after cutting it? The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not kill him; for if you kill him he shall be in your position before you kill him, and you shall be in his position before he says the word he said."
"18764","587 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi then al-Junda'i, that 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him, that al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr al-Kindi - an ally of Banu Zuhrah who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - narrated to him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, if I meet a man of the disbelievers and we fight and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: I have submitted to Allah - shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he says it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not kill him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands, then said it after cutting it - shall I kill him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not kill him; for if you kill him, he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he says the word he said."
"18765","588 - Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab informed me, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar, who informed him, that al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: What do you think of a man of the disbelievers who fights me and we exchange two blows, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: I have submitted - shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he says it? He said: Do not kill him; for if you kill him he shall be in your position before you kill him, and you shall be in his position before he says the word he said."
"18766","589 - Ahmad ibn 'Anbar al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated, al-Zuhri narrated, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr al-Kindi - who witnessed Badr - that he informed him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the disbelievers and fight him and he cuts off my hand, then takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: I have submitted to Allah - shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he says it? He said: Do not kill him; for if you kill him, you are in his position before he says the word he said."
"18767","590 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-'Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated, from his father, from Ibn Shihab, 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Junda'i informed me, that 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him, from al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - a man of Kindah, ally of Banu Zuhrah - that he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the disbelievers and I and he exchange two blows and he strikes me and severs one of my hands, then I strike him, then I gain power to kill him, and he says when I am about to raise my weapon to him: There is no god but Allah - shall I kill him or leave him? He said: No, rather leave him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands? He said: Even if he did. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands? He said: Even if he did. I repeated to him, and he said: If you kill him after he says: There is no god but Allah, then you are in his position before he says it, and he is in your position before you kill him."
"18768","591 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi then al-Junda'i narrated to me, that 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him, that al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr al-Kindi - an ally of Banu Zuhrah who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - informed him, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the disbelievers and we fight and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off - then he mentioned the like of it."
"18769","592 - 'Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Uzayz al-Ayli narrated, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated, from 'Uqayl, Ibn Shihab informed me, that 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi then al-Junda'i informed him, that 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him, that al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr al-Kindi, ally of Banu Zuhrah, said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the disbelievers and he fights me and strikes one of my hands and cuts it off, then takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: I have submitted to Allah - shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not kill him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands, then said that after cutting it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you kill him, you are in his position before he says the word he said, and he is in your position before you kill him."
"18770","593 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, from Salih ibn Kaysan, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, that 'Ata' ibn Yazid informed him, that 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi informed him, that al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr informed him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the polytheists and he fights me and strikes one of my hands and cuts it off, then takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: I have submitted to Allah - shall I kill him after he says it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not kill him after he says it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands then said that after cutting it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you kill him, he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he says the word he said."
"18771","594 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd narrated, my uncle narrated, Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri narrated, from his uncle, 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi then al-Junda'i informed me, that 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him, that al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr - an ally of Banu Zuhrah who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - informed him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man of the disbelievers and we fight and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: I have submitted to Allah - shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he says it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not kill him; for if you kill him, he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he says the word he said."
"18772","595 - Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, al-Awza'i narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I met a man of the polytheists and he cut off my hand, then took refuge from me behind a tree and said: I have submitted to Allah - then he mentioned the like of the hadith before it."
"18773","Sulayman ibn Yasar, from al-Miqdad. 596 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, (ha) and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik, (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated; all of them from Malik ibn Anas, from Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from al-Miqdad, that 'Ali commanded him to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who draws near his wife so that madhiy comes out of him: what is due upon him? For his daughter is with me and I am shy to ask him. Al-Miqdad said: So I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: When one of you finds that, let him sprinkle (water on) his private part and perform his ablution for prayer."
"18774","Abu al-Mu'arik al-Misri, from al-Miqdad. 597 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to me, 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from 'Ayyash ibn 'Abbas, from Abu al-Mu'arik, that a man of Ghafiq had a claim of one hundred dinars upon a man of Mahrah in the time of 'Uthman; they gained a fine spoil. The Mahri said: I shall hasten seventy dinars to you on condition that you cancel the hundred from me - and the hundred was disputed - so the Ghafiqi accepted that. Al-Miqdad passed by them and took hold of his mount's bridle to witness it; when he told him the account he said: Both of you have been proclaimed with war from Allah and His Messenger (i.e. for usury/discount settlement)."
"18775","Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad. 598 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him, from his father, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad came to us for a need of his; we said: Sit, may Allah keep you well, until your need is sought. He said: I wonder at people I just passed by who wish for tribulation, claiming that Allah may test them therein as He tested His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions. By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The fortunate is indeed he who is spared tribulations - repeating it three times - and if he is tested and remains patient. By Allah, I shall not testify for anyone to Paradise until I know what he dies upon, after a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The heart of the son of Adam turns over more swiftly than a pot when it boils fully."
"18776","599 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, 'Abdullah ibn Salim narrated, from Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The heart of the son of Adam turns over more swiftly than a pot when it boils fully."
"18777","600 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated; both said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Safwan ibn 'Amr, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father, who said: We sat with al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad one day when a man passed by him - and I listened - and said: Blessed are these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, I wish we had seen what you saw and witnessed what you witnessed. He turned to him and said: What makes a man wish for a presence that Allah kept him away from, not knowing how he would have been in it had he witnessed it? By Allah, peoples attended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whom Allah cast down on their nostrils into Hell for not answering him and not believing him. Will Allah not spare any of you? Do you not recognize the blessings of your Lord, believing in what your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought? You have been spared trial through others. By Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was indeed sent in the harshest condition in which a prophet was sent: in an interval (between prophets) and ignorance, when they saw no religion better than idol-worship. Then he came with a criterion separating truth from falsehood, and separating father from his son, until a man would see his father or his son or his brother a disbeliever - though Allah had opened the lock of his heart with faith - knowing that whoever enters the Fire has perished, so his eye finds no joy while knowing his loved one is in the Fire. And it is that which Allah Almighty said: (Our Lord, grant us from our spouses and offspring comfort of eyes)."
"18778","Salim ibn 'Amir Abu Yahya al-Kala'i, from al-Miqdad. 601 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, that he heard Sulaym ibn 'Amir narrating, that he heard al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall not remain upon the face of the earth a house of mud-brick nor of hair (tent) except that Allah shall bring Islam into it, with the might of one mighty or the humiliation of one humbled: either He honors them and guides them to Islam, or He humbles them so they pay the jizyah."
"18779","602 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, (ha) and Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated; both of them from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, Sulaym ibn 'Amir narrated to me, al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sun shall be brought near on the Day of Resurrection to the creation until it is from them at a distance of a mil - Sulaym said: By Allah, I do not know what he meant by mil: a distance of the earth, or the mil (stylus) with which the eye is lined with kohl? - He said: People shall be in sweat according to their deeds: among them he who is up to his ankles, among them he who is up to his knees, among them he who is up to his waist, and among them he whom sweat bridles. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed to his mouth."
"18780","603 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, (ha) and 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated; both said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated, from Sulaym ibn 'Amir, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: I shall not say of anyone good or evil until I see with what his deed is sealed, after something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And what did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The heart of the son of Adam turns over more violently than a pot when it boils fully."
"18781","604 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ashkib al-Kufi narrated, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from Yazid ibn Sinan Abu Farwah, from Abu Yahya al-Kala'i, from Sulaym ibn 'Amir, al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People shall be gathered, from the miscarried fetus to the aged elder, as sons of thirty-three: in the form of Adam, the beauty of Yusuf, and the character of Ayyub, lined with kohl, with flowing locks."
"18782","Abu Zabyah al-Kala'i, from al-Miqdad. 605 - Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated, (ha) and 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated, (ha) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ashkib al-Kufi narrated, (ha) and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated; all said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Ansari narrated, saying: I heard Abu Zabyah al-Kala'i say: I heard al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad narrate that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked them about adultery, and they said: Forbidden; Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it. He said: That a man commit adultery with ten women is better for him than that he commit adultery with his neighbor's wife. He said: And he asked them about theft, and they said: Forbidden; Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it. He said: That a man steal from ten houses is easier upon him than that he steal from his neighbor's house."
"18783","Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd al-Hadrami, from al-Miqdad. 606 - Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn 'Utbah narrated, (ha) and 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn 'Asim narrated to me; both said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Safwan ibn 'Amr, from Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves Allah and His Messenger truthfully, not falsely, and meets the believers and loves them, and the affair of pre-Islamic ignorance is to him like the station of a fire cast into it - then he has tasted the flavor of faith - or he said: then he has reached the peak of faith - the doubt is from Safwan."
"18784","'Amr ibn al-Aswad, from al-Miqdad. 607 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah Abu Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr and 'Amr ibn al-Aswad, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad and Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the imam seeks tribulation among the people, he corrupts them."
"18785","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from al-Miqdad. 608 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Kindi al-Himsi narrated to me, 'Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar narrated, Hariz ibn 'Uthman narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, who said: People - or a man - passed by al-Miqdad and said: How fortunate are these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Miqdad gathered in anger and said: O people, do not wish for a matter that Allah has kept away; how many saw him but did not benefit from seeing him."
"18786","'Umayr ibn Ishaq, from al-Miqdad. 609 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-'Abbas al-Narsi narrated to me, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated; both said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, 'Abdullah ibn 'Awn narrated, from 'Umayr ibn Ishaq, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an expedition; when I returned he said to me: How do you find yourself? I said: I have not ceased until I thought I had dependents with me. By Allah, I shall never work (as a leader) over two men after it, ever."
"18787","Duba'ah bint al-Miqdad, from her father. 610 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Ayyash narrated, al-Walid ibn Kamil Abu 'Ubaydah al-Bajali narrated, from al-Muhallab ibn Hujr al-Nahrani, from Duba'ah bint al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, from her father, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray toward a pillar, nor a stick, nor a tree, except that he placed it at his right eyebrow-side or his left eyebrow-side, and he did not face it squarely."
"18788","Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, wife of al-Miqdad, from al-Miqdad. 611 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated, my paternal aunt Quraybah bint 'Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to me, from her mother Karimah bint al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr - who was under al-Miqdad - who said: People used to go out for their need only once every two or three days, and would drop dung like camels drop dung. One day al-Miqdad went out for his need until he reached al-Khakhbah - in Baqi' al-Gharqad - and entered a ruin for his need. While he was sitting, a rat came out of a hole with a dinar; it kept bringing out dinar after dinar until it reached seventeen dinars. I went out with them until I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of its news, and he said: Did you follow your hand into the hole? I said: No, by Him who sent you with the truth. He said: There is no charity due upon you in it; may Allah bless it for you. Duba'ah said: Its last did not run out until I saw locks of silver in the house of al-Miqdad."
"18789","612 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to me, from his paternal aunt Quraybah bint 'Abdillah, from her mother Karimah bint al-Miqdad, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr, that she informed him, saying: al-Miqdad went for his need and entered a ruin, when the rat brought out of a hole dinar after dinar, until it brought out seventeen dinars; then it brought out the edge of a green rag. Al-Miqdad said: So I stood and pulled the edge of the rag and found in it a dinar, making eighteen dinars. Al-Miqdad went with them and sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he informed him of its news and said: Take its charity, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you reach with your hand into the hole? Al-Miqdad said: No, by Him who sent you with the truth. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Miqdad: May Allah bless it for you."
"18790","613 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated; both said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated, Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated, my paternal aunt Quraybah bint 'Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to me, from her mother Karimah bint al-Miqdad, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib - who was under al-Miqdad - from al-Miqdad, who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Something I heard from you has made me doubt. He said: When one of you doubts in a matter, let him ask me about it. He said: Your saying about your wives: I hope for them after me the truthful ones. He said: And whom do you count as the truthful ones? We said: Our children who perish young. He said: But the truthful ones are the charitable ones. He said it three times."
"18791","614 - Hajjaj ibn 'Imran al-Sadusi al-Basri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated, Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Waqidi narrated, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated, from his paternal aunt Quraybah bint 'Abdillah ibn Wahb, from her mother Karimah bint al-Miqdad, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, from al-Miqdad ibn 'Amr, that he was on the day of Badr upon a horse called Subhah; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted for him a share for his horse and a share for him."
"18792","Al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib al-Kindi, kunyah Abu Karimah; and it is said: Abu Yahya; he settled in Syria and died there. 615 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Muslim, that Khalid ibn Yazid said to al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib: O Abu Karimah."
"18793","616 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us, Shabab al-'Usfuri narrated, saying: al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, kunyah Abu Yahya; al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib died in the year eighty-seven at ninety-one years of age."
"18794","617 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Muslim, who said: I saw five of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trimming their mustaches, leaving their beards and dyeing them yellow, among them al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib."
"18795","618 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, Abu Tarafah 'Abbad ibn al-Rayyan al-Lakhmi al-Himsi narrated, saying: I came to al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib while he was in a village some miles from Hims on a festival day; we said: Come out and lead us in the festival prayer. He said: No; pray individually."
"18796","619 - Al-Husayn ibn Taqi ibn Abi Taqi al-Himsi narrated to us, my grandfather Abu Taqi Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated, from Humayd ibn Rabi'ah al-Qurashi, who said: I saw Abu Umamah al-Bahili and al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib wearing two hooded cloaks (burnus)."
"18797","620 - Musa ibn 'Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, my father narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Rashid, who said: I heard al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - while most people say: the Decree is in a hundred years, meaning after a hundred years the Hour comes - and al-Miqdam said: You have said much; Allah shall not be incapable of delaying this ummah half a day - meaning five hundred years."
"18798","Al-Sha'bi, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib. 621 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, (ha) and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, both said: Abu Nu'aym narrated; both said: Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Miqdam Abu Karimah al-Shami, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guest's night (of hospitality) is a due right, obligatory upon every Muslim; if he (the guest) wakes in his courtyard (unhosted), it is a debt upon him: if he wishes he claims it, and if he wishes he leaves it."
"18799","622 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah informed, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Karimah, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The guest's night (of hospitality) is a right upon every Muslim; and whoever the guest wakes in his courtyard, it is a right or a debt: if he wishes he claims it, and if he wishes he leaves it."
"18800","623 - Al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated, (ha) and 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, (ha) and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated; all said: Abu 'Awanah narrated, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Karimah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The guest's night (of hospitality) is obligatory upon every Muslim; whoever wakes in his courtyard, it is for him a debt upon him: if he wishes he claims, and if he wishes he leaves."
"18801","624 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' and Jarir narrated, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Miqdam Abu Karimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guest's night (of hospitality) is a right; if he wakes in his courtyard it is a debt upon him: if he wishes he claims it, and if he wishes he leaves it."
"18802","Abu 'Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam. 625 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (ha) and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated; both said: Shu'bah narrated, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, who said: I heard 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abu 'Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves a burden (dependents/debt), it is to Allah and to His Messenger - or he said: to us; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs; and I am the heir of him who has no heir: I inherit his wealth and release his captive; and the maternal uncle is the client of him who has no client: he inherits his wealth and releases his captive."
"18803","626 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, (ha) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both said: Musaddad narrated; both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abu 'Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam al-Kindi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am closer to every believer than his own self; whoever leaves a debt or a neglected family, it is to me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs; and I am the guardian of him who has no guardian: I inherit his wealth and release his captive; and the maternal uncle is the client of him who has no client: he inherits his wealth and releases his captive."
"18804","627 - 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq narrated to us, my father narrated, (ha) and 'Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated, 'Abd al-Warith narrated, 'Abdullah ibn Salim informed, from al-Zubaydi, Rashid ibn Sa'd narrated, from Ibn 'A'idh, who narrated to him, that al-Miqdam narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves a debt or a neglected family, it is to me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heir; and I am the client of him who has no client: I release his captive and inherit his wealth; and the maternal uncle is the client of him who has no client: he releases his captive and inherits his wealth."
"18805","628 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib al-Kindi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever leaves a debt or a neglected family, it is to me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs; and I am the client of him who has no client: I release his captive and inherit his wealth."
"18806","Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam. 629 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The martyr has with Allah nine qualities - or he said: ten qualities: he is forgiven at the first shedding of his blood, he sees his seat in Paradise, he is adorned with the ornament of faith, he is protected from the punishment of the grave, he is married to wide-eyed houris, he is safe on the day of the greatest terror, a crown of dignity is placed on his head - a single ruby of it is better than the world and what is in it - he is married to ninety-two wives of the wide-eyed houris, and he intercedes for seventy persons of his relatives."
"18807","630 - Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding upon the skins of predators."
"18808","631 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No one ever ate food better than eating from the work of his hand; and Dawud (David) ate only from the work of his hand."
"18809","632 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi and Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhalam al-Dimashqi narrated to us, both said: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesturing with his hand, saying: None of you eats food in this world better for him than eating from the work of his hands."
"18810","633 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated, al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one of the children of Adam ever ate food better for him than eating from the work of his hands - the Prophet of Allah said - and Dawud (David, peace be upon him) used to eat from the work of his hands."
"18811","634 - Al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whatever you feed your wife is charity for you; whatever you feed your child is charity for you; whatever you feed your servant is charity for you; and whatever you feed yourself is charity for you."
"18812","635 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasan is of me, and Husayn is of 'Ali."
"18813","636 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who said: al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib and 'Amr ibn al-Aswad - a man of al-Asad of the people of Qinnasrin, of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - came as a delegation to Mu'awiyah (may Allah have mercy on him). Mu'awiyah said to al-Miqdam: Did you not know that al-Hasan ibn 'Ali has died? Al-Miqdam said: So al-Miqdam uttered istirja' (We belong to Allah and to Him we return). Mu'awiyah said to him: Do you consider it a calamity? He said: Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed him in his lap and said: This is of me, and Husayn is of 'Ali. Then he said to the Asadi: What do you say? He said: A coal that Allah has extinguished. Al-Miqdam said: As for me, I shall not leave until I anger you today and make you hear what you dislike. Then he said: If I am truthful, confirm me; and if I lie, belie me. He said: I shall. He said: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid wearing gold? He said: Yes. He said: And I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the skins of predators and riding upon them? He said: Yes. He said: By Allah, I have seen all of this in your house, O Mu'awiyah. Mu'awiyah said: I knew I would not escape it today, O Miqdam. Khalid said: And Mu'awiyah ordered wealth for him, but did not order for his companion; and he assigned a stipend for his son. He said: Al-Miqdam distributed it among his companions and gave the Asadi nothing of what he took. That reached Mu'awiyah, who said: As for al-Miqdam, he is a generous man, open-handed; as for the Asadi, he is a man good at withholding for himself."
"18814","637 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated, (ha) and Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated; all said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, (ha) and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, from Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your fathers; Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your mothers; Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) the nearest, then the nearest."
"18815","638 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty enjoins upon you (duties toward) your mothers - three times - Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your fathers - twice - Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) the nearest, then the nearest."
"18816","639 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Thawr, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your mothers; Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your mothers; Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your fathers; Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) the nearest, then the nearest."
"18817","640 - Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn Khalaf al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, Umm 'Abdillah bint Khalid ibn Ma'dan narrated to me, from her father, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib al-Kindi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your mothers; Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your mothers; Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) your fathers; Allah enjoins upon you (duties toward) the nearest, then the nearest."
"18818","641 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Hold to sahur (the pre-dawn meal), for it is the blessed nourishment."
"18819","642 - Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhalam al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated, from his father, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that he was on campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they alighted beside enclosures of Jews at Khaybar, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took from them. The Jews went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained of that to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Khalid ibn al-Walid, who proclaimed: Prayer in congregation; none shall enter Paradise but a Muslim. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: What is lawful for you of the property of the covenanted peoples without right? They say: Whatever we find in the Book of Allah as lawful, we deem lawful; and whatever we find therein as unlawful, we deem unlawful. Lo, I forbid the property of the covenanted peoples, and every fanged beast of prey, and what is used of riding animals except what Allah has named."
"18820","643 - Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhalam narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Measure your food; it shall be blessed for you."
"18821","Yahya ibn Jabir al-Ta'i, from al-Miqdam. 644 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Hawtiyyan narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym al-Kattani narrated, Yahya ibn Jabir narrated to me, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib al-Kindi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No son of Adam ever fills a vessel worse than the belly; sufficient for the son of Adam are morsels that straighten his back; if he must, then a third for food, a third for drink, and a third for his breath."
"18822","645 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam never fills a vessel worse than the belly; sufficient for the Muslim are morsels that straighten his back; if he must, then a third for his food, a third for his drink, and a third for his breath."
"18823","646 - Isma'il ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym al-Kinani and Habib ibn Salih, from Yahya ibn Jabir al-Ta'i, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"18824","647 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym al-Kinani, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seek refuge in Allah from greed that leads to miserliness, and from greed that leads to what is unattainable."
"18825","648 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated; both said: Muhammad ibn Harb narrated, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Allah enjoins upon you good toward women; Allah enjoins upon you good toward women, for they are your mothers, your daughters and your maternal aunts. A man of the People of the Book marries a woman while her hands cannot yet tie a thread, yet neither of them desires to leave the other."
"18826","Al-Hasan ibn Jabir, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib. 649 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Jabir narrated, that he heard al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade things on the day of Khaybar, among them domestic donkeys and other things. He said: And soon a man reclining on his couch, narrated a hadith of mine, shall say: Between us and you is the Book of Allah; whatever we find therein as lawful we deem lawful, and as unlawful we deem unlawful. Lo, what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has forbidden is like what Allah Almighty has forbidden."
"18827","650 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from al-Hasan ibn Jabir, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade things, until he mentioned domestic donkeys."
"18828","Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd al-Hadrami, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib. 651 - Al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib and Abu Umamah, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam pursues suspicion among the people, he corrupts them."
"18829","652 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, my father narrated to me, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Miqdam, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man shall be over a people except that he comes leading them on the Day of Resurrection, with a banner before him that he carries while they follow him; he shall be questioned about them and they shall be questioned about him."
"18830","653 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, my father narrated to me, from Damdam ibn Zur'ah, from Shurayh ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib and Abu Umamah al-Bahili, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this affair is among your people, so enjoin them concerning us. He said to them: I remind you of Allah: do not transgress against my ummah after me. Then he said to the people: There shall be rulers after me, so render them obedience; for the ruler is like a shield, protection is sought by him. If they do right and command you to good, it is for you and for them; and if they do evil in what they command you, it is upon them and you are free of it. When the ruler pursues suspicion among the people, he corrupts them."
"18831","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib. 654 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Abu Zayd al-Hawtiyyan narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Hariz ibn 'Uthman narrated, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah narrated to me, saying: I heard al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib say: Ablution water was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he performed ablution: he washed his hands three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his forearms three times; he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times each, then wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner sides, and washed his feet three times each."
"18832","655 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Hariz ibn 'Uthman narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"18833","656 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ka'b al-Halabi narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Hariz ibn 'Uthman, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution; when he reached wiping the head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then passed them until he reached the nape, then returned them to the place from which he began."
"18834","657 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated, my father narrated, Hariz ibn 'Uthman narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah, who said: A man passed by al-Miqdam and said: How fortunate are these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Miqdam gathered in anger and said: O people, do not wish for a matter that Allah has kept away from you."
"18835","Habib ibn 'Ubayd al-Rahabi, from al-Miqdam. 658 - 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated, (ha) and 'Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-'Utbi narrated to us, both said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated, 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, al-Fudayl ibn Fadalah narrated to me, that Habib ibn 'Ubayd narrated to him, that al-Miqdam narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Obey your rulers whatever may be; if they command you to something of what I brought you, they are rewarded for it and you are rewarded for obeying them; and if they command you to something of what I did not bring you, it is upon them and you are free of it. That is because when you meet Allah you shall say: Our Lord, no injustice; and He shall say: No injustice. Then you shall say: Our Lord, You sent messengers to us and we obeyed them by Your leave; You appointed successors over us and we obeyed them by Your leave; and You set rulers over us and we obeyed them for You. And He shall say: You have spoken the truth; it is upon them, and you are free of it."
"18836","659 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Irq al-Yahsabi al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Miqdam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There shall come upon people a time: whoever has with him neither gold nor silver shall not enjoy life."
"18837","660 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Waki'i narrated to us, Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated, Baqiyyah narrated, 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Zubaydi narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated, from Habib ibn 'Ubayd, who said: I saw al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib sitting in the market, with a slave-girl of his selling milk while he sat taking the dirhams. He was questioned about that, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When it is the end of time, people shall inevitably need dirhams and dinars therein; a man upholds by them his religion and his worldly life."
"18838","661 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Thawr ibn Yazid, Habib ibn 'Ubayd narrated to me, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib al-Kindi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you loves his brother, let him inform him of that."
"18839","662 - Al-Hasan ibn al-'Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated, Hassan ibn Hassan narrated, from Hariz ibn 'Uthman, from Habib ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one ever fills a vessel worse than the belly; if his soul overcomes him, let him leave a third for his breath."
"18840","Salim ibn 'Amir al-Khaba'iri, from him. 663 - 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (ha) and 'Umarah ibn Wathimah al-Misri and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-'Utbi narrated, both said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated, 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Salim, from al-Zubaydi, Salim ibn 'Amir narrated, that al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who dies, whether miscarried or aged - and people are but in between that - except that he is raised as a son of thirty years: whoever is of the people of Paradise shall be upon the form of Adam, the image of Yusuf, and the heart of Ayyub; and whoever is of the people of the Fire shall be magnified and swollen like mountains."
"18841","664 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan al-Raqqi narrated, (ha) and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Bazzar al-Asbahani narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated; both said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, Yazid ibn Sinan narrated, Abu Yahya Salim ibn 'Amir al-Kala'i narrated, saying: We said to al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib al-Kindi: O Abu Karimah, people claim you did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes indeed, by Allah, I saw him; he even took the lobe of this ear of mine while I was walking with an uncle of mine, then he said to my uncle: Do you think he will remember it? We said: O Abu Karimah, narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard him say: From the miscarried fetus to the aged elder shall be gathered on the Day of Resurrection in the form of Adam, the heart of Ayyub, and the beauty of Yusuf, hairless, lined with kohl. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what of the disbeliever? He said: He is magnified for the Fire until the thickness of his skin becomes forty cubits, and the molar tooth among his teeth like Uhud."
"18842","665 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated, my father narrated, from his father, Abu Yahya al-Kala'i narrated, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guest's night (of hospitality) is a due right, obligatory; if he wakes deprived in his courtyard, his support becomes obligatory upon the Muslims until they take for him his right from their crops and livestock, for what he was deprived of his right of hospitality."
"18843","666 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, 'Umar ibn Khath'am narrated, Salim ibn 'Amir narrated to me, from al-Miqdam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun shall draw near people on the Day of Resurrection until it is from people at a distance of two mils, and its heat shall increase and scorch them; they shall be in sweat according to their deeds: among them he whom sweat takes to his ankles, among them he whom it takes to his knees, among them he whom it takes to his waist, and among them he whom sweat bridles. He said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesture with his hands toward his mouth. Ibrahim ibn 'Irq said: Thus 'Umar ibn Khath'am narrated it, from Sulaym, from al-Miqdam."
"18844","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi 'Awf al-Jurashi, from al-Miqdam. 667 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from al-Zubaydi, (ha) and Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated, al-Qasim ibn Musa narrated, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, Marwan ibn Ru'bah narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi 'Awf al-Jurashi, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whenever a man stays as guest with a people and they do not host him, he is entitled to claim from them the like of his hospitality."
"18845","668 - Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, 'Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar narrated, from Hariz ibn 'Uthman, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi 'Awf, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever alights with a people, it is upon them to host him; if they do not host him, he is entitled to penalize them with the like of his hospitality."
"18846","669 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi narrated to me, from 'Amr ibn Ru'bah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi 'Awf al-Jurashi, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given the Book and its equal; soon a satiated man on his couch shall say: Between us and you is this Book; whatever therein is lawful we deem lawful, and whatever therein is unlawful we deem unlawful. Lo, it is not so: no fanged beast of prey is lawful, nor domestic donkeys, nor the lost property of a covenanted person except that he has no need of it; and whenever a man stays as guest with a people and they do not host him, he is entitled to take from them by force the like of his hospitality."
"18847","670 - Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Ayyash al-Himsi narrated, (ha) and Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated; both said: Hariz ibn 'Uthman narrated, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Bahr narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Hariz ibn 'Uthman narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi 'Awf, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given the Book and its like; lo, soon a satiated man on his couch shall say: Hold to the Qur'an; whatever you find therein as lawful, deem it lawful; and whatever you find therein as unlawful, deem it unlawful. Lo, the domestic donkey is not lawful for you, nor every fanged beast of prey, nor the lost property of a covenanted person except that its owner has no need of it; and whoever alights with a people, it is upon them to host him."
"18848","Rashid ibn Sa'd, from al-Miqdam. 671 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated, Maslamah ibn 'Ulayy narrated, al-Zubaydi narrated, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall conquer horizons wherein are houses called bathhouses; entry into them is forbidden for my ummah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, they remove fatigue and cleanse dirt. He said: They are lawful for the males of my ummah in waist-wrappers, forbidden for the females of my ummah."
"18849","Those named Muttalib. Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hisham ibn 'Abd Manaf; and it is said: 'Abd al-Muttalib, and the correct is: al-Muttalib; he died in Damascus, where he lived, in the year sixty-one. 672 - Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Shibami narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated, al-Thawri informed, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'ah, (ha) and 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated, my father 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib entered upon him angry. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is with us and Quraysh? When they meet among themselves they meet with cheerful faces, and when they meet us they meet us otherwise? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until his face reddened. He said: Faith shall not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for Allah and His Messenger. A man's paternal uncle is the like of his father."
"18850","673 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Marwan al-Kufi narrated, 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah, who said: al-'Abbas entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Quraysh meet with radiant faces and meet us otherwise. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until the vein between his eyes filled. Then he said: No servant shall taste the flavor of faith until he loves you for Allah and for His Messenger."
"18851","674 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Yazid narrated from Jarir from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabiʿah, he said: Al-Abbas came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while angry, so he said: What brought you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is with us and Quraysh? He said: What is with you and them that brought you? He said: Some of them meet others with radiant faces, but when they meet us they meet us otherwise. So he became angry until a vein between his eyes swelled, then when it was relieved from him he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, faith does not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for Allah and His Messenger. Then he said: What is with men who harm me regarding Al-Abbas? For the paternal uncle of a man is like his father."
"18852","675 - Saʿid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Misri narrated to us: Saʿid ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, (H) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated, both said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from al-Muttalib ibn Rabiʿah ibn al-Harith, he said: Some people from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we hear harshness from some people; one of them says: The likeness of Muhammad is only like a palm tree grown in a dunghill. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: O people, who am I? They said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: I am Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib - we never heard him claim lineage before it - Allah created creation and made me from the best of His creation, then made them two groups and made me in the better of the two groups, then made them tribes and made me from the best tribe among them, then made them houses and made me in the best house; so I am the best of you in house and the best of you in person."
"18853","676 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabiʿah, that some people from the Ansar said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We hear from some people of Quraysh until one of them says: The likeness of Muhammad is only like a palm tree planted in a dunghill. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, who am I? They said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: I am Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib - they said: we never heard him claim lineage before it at all - then he said: Allah created creation then divided them into two groups and made me from the better of the two groups, then made them tribes and made me from the best tribe among them; so I am the best of you in house and the best of you in person."
"18854","677 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid informed us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Abdullah ibn Rabiʿah from Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabiʿah, he said: The sons of Abd al-Muttalib gathered and said: Why do you not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to assign to you what he assigned to the sons of so-and-so, to assign to you the collection of alms? So they met Ali and spoke to him, and he said: Allah Almighty and His Messenger refuse for you to take the filth of peoples hands - or he said: the washings of peoples hands. Abd al-Muttalib said to his father: Send me, so Al-Abbas sent his son Al-Fadl. So we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and entered, and each one of us spoke privately, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What have you concealed here? I said: O Messenger of Allah, your people and cousins sent us for you to assign to them what you assigned to the people of alms-collection. He said: Allah and His Messenger refuse that for you, that you eat the filth - or he said: the washings - of peoples hands."
"18855","678 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabiʿah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: Al-Abbas sent his son Al-Fadl, and my father Rabiʿah ibn al-Harith sent me, so we went until we entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"18856","Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah al-Sahmi, and he is al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah ibn Subayrah ibn Saʿid ibn Saʿd ibn Sahm ibn Amr ibn Husays ibn Kaʿb ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr; he accepted Islam on the day of the Conquest. 679 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from Abd al-Razzaq from Maʿmar from Ibn Tawus from Ikrimah ibn Khalid from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in al-Najm, and the people prostrated with him. Al-Muttalib said: And I did not prostrate with them - and he was then a polytheist. Al-Muttalib said: So I will never leave prostrating in it ever."
"18857","680 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from Abd al-Razzaq from Amr ibn Qays: Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah al-Sahmi informed me from his father from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the Sacred Mosque while the people were circumambulating the House between him and the qiblah, in front of him, with no screen between him and them."
"18858","681 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Uyaynah from Kathir ibn Kathir from his father from his grandfather, the like of it, except he said: I saw him praying on the side of the door of Banu Sahm."
"18859","682 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us: Saʿid ibn Abi Maryam narrated: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated from Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah from his father from al-Muttalib, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying toward the House with no one between him and the circumambulation."
"18860","683 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated: al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed us, (H) and al-Muttalib ibn Shuʿayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated: al-Layth narrated to me from Ibn Jurayj from Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib from his father Kathir from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at the edge of the circumambulation area with no screen between him and the circumambulation. This is the wording of Ibn Salih; and Ibn Abd al-Hakam said in his hadith: He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he finished his saʿy pray at the edge of the circumambulation area with no screen between him and those circumambulating."
"18861","684 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Ibn Jurayj: Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib narrated to me from his father: The notables of al-Muttalib narrated to me from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying facing the Corner while men were passing in front of him."
"18862","685 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated: Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuʿayb narrated from Hisham ibn Hassan from Salim ibn Abdullah from Kathir ibn al-Muttalib from his father from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the Kaʿbah and stood facing the Corner and prayed two rakʿahs while the people were passing in front of him circumambulating the House: men and women. This Salim ibn Abdullah is Salim al-Khayyat."
"18863","686 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hatim ibn Isa narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: Amr ibn Dinar narrated from Abbad ibn al-Muttalib from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray facing the Corner near the watering place while men and women were passing in front of him."
"18864","687 - Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us: Safwan ibn Salih narrated: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated: Salim al-Khayyat and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated: Kathir ibn Kathir narrated to us from his father: al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah narrated to me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying parallel to the Black Corner while men and women were passing in front of him with no screen between him and them."
"18865","688 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati and Saʿid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Misri narrated to us, both said: Saʿid ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated from Salih ibn Umar: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated from al-Zuhri from al-Saib ibn Yazid from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man sitting and said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. So the people exerted themselves to stand."
"18866","689 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated: Abu Shihab narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abu Salih from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a vessel of nabidh, so he poured water over it until it overflowed, then he drank from it."
"18867","690 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from al-Kalbi from Abu Salih from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaʿah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House on a hot summer day and became thirsty and sought drink. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a drink from these raisins, shall I give you some? He said: Yes. So the man sent to his house and a great cup was brought. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought it close to his mouth and found it had a strong smell, so he disliked it and returned it."
"18868","One named Mutiʿ: Mutiʿ ibn al-Aswad al-Adawi al-Qurashi, and he is Mutiʿ ibn al-Aswad ibn Harithah ibn Nadlah ibn Jurayyan ibn Awf ibn Ubayd Uwayj ibn Adi ibn Kaʿb; his mother is al-Ajma bint Yaman ibn al-Fadl ibn Afif ibn Kalb ibn Hasasah al-Khuzaʿi. 691 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of al-Maghazi, narrated: Ibrahim ibn Saʿd narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Shuʿbah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar from Amir al-Shaʿbi from Abdullah ibn Mutiʿ ibn al-Aswad from his father Mutiʿ - and his name was al-As, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Mutiʿ - he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he killed these men saying: Makkah will not be raided after this year, and no one of Quraysh will be killed as a captive after this year."
"18869","692 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated: Qays ibn al-Rabiʿ narrated from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah from al-Shaʿbi from Abdullah ibn Mutiʿ ibn al-Aswad from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Conquest: No Qurashi will be killed as a captive after this day."
"18870","693 - Muʿadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Yahya ibn Zakariya narrated from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah: Amir narrated from Abdullah ibn Mutiʿ, he said: I heard Mutiʿ saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying: No Qurashi will be killed as a captive after this day until the Day of Resurrection. And none of the disobedient ones of Quraysh attained Islam except Mutiʿ, and his name was al-As, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Mutiʿ."
"18871","694 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated: Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated: my father narrated to me from al-Shaʿbi from Abdullah ibn Mutiʿ, he said: I heard Mutiʿ saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"18872","695 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated: Isa ibn Yunus narrated from Mujalid from al-Shaʿbi from Ibn Mutiʿ from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Conquest: It is not proper that a Qurashi be killed as a captive after this day of mine."
"18873","One named Mihjan: Mihjan Abu Busr al-Dayli. 696 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuʿaym narrated: Sufyan narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from Bishr ibn Mihjan al-Dili from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I had prayed among my family, then the prayer was established and I sat. When he prayed he said: Are you not a Muslim? I said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from praying with the people? He said: I had prayed among my family. He said: Then pray with the people even if you had prayed among your family. Thus Sufyan narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam from Bishr ibn Mihjan, and he erred in it; it is rather Busr ibn Mihjan, thus Malik and the companions of Zayd ibn Aslam narrated it."
"18874","697 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabi narrated from Malik, (H) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated: Malik narrated, (H) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated: Malik informed us, (H) and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanʿani narrated to us: Ismaʿil ibn Abi Uways narrated: Malik narrated to me from Zayd ibn Aslam from a man of Banu al-Dil called Busr ibn Mihjan from his father, that he was in a gathering with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was called for prayer, so he stood and prayed with them, then he returned while Mihjan was in his seat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevented you from praying with the people? Are you not a Muslim man? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but I prayed among my family. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When you come, pray with the people even if you had prayed."
"18875","698 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Jurayj and Dawud ibn Qays from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibn Mihjan al-Dili from his father, he said: I prayed Zuhr - or Asr - in my house, then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat by him, then the prayer was established, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and I did not pray. When he finished he said: Are you not a Muslim? I said: Yes. He said: What is with you that you did not pray? I said: I had prayed in my house. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, pray, even if you had prayed."
"18876","699 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Maʿmar informed us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Busr ibn Mihjan from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke to him about a need, then the prayer was established while I was sitting, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed. Then he finished and found me sitting, so he said to me: Are you not a Muslim? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What prevented you from praying with us? I said: I prayed in my lodging. He said: Even if you had prayed in your lodging."
"18877","700 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, both said: al-Qaʿnabi narrated: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from Busr ibn Mihjan from his father, he said: I prayed Zuhr - or Asr - in my house, then I went out to the mosque and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting with people around him, so I sat with them. Then the prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and prayed for the people, then he came out and found me sitting in my seat where he had seen me. So he said: Are you not a Muslim man? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I am a Muslim. He said: What prevented you from entering and praying with the people? I said: I had prayed among my family. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you have prayed among your family, then you come to the mosque and find the people praying, pray with them."
"18878","701 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us: Saʿid ibn Abi Maryam narrated: Muhammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam: Busr ibn Mihjan informed me from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"18879","702 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Saʿid narrated: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from Busr ibn Mihjan from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"18880","Mihjan ibn al-Adraʿ al-Sulami. 703 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Maʿmar al-Muqʿad narrated: Abd al-Warith narrated: Husayn al-Muʿallim narrated from Abdullah ibn Yazid: Hanzalah ibn Ali narrated to me that Mihjan ibn al-Adraʿ narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and there was a man who had finished his prayer while reciting the tashahhud, saying: O Allah, I ask You by Allah, the One, the Eternal, Who did not beget and was not begotten, and there is none like Him, to forgive me my sins; indeed You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has been forgiven, he has been forgiven, he has been forgiven."
"18881","704 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuʿayb al-Simsar narrated to us: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated, both said: Abu Awanah narrated from Abu Bishr from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Raja ibn Abi Raja al-Bahili from Mihjan ibn al-Adraʿ, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold until we ascended Uhud, and he overlooked Madinah. He said: Woe to it as a town whose people will leave it at its most flourishing; the Dajjal will come to it and find at every pass of its passes an angel with drawn sword. Then he descended until he came to the mosque, and there was a man standing praying and reciting. He said: Do you see him, Abdullah ibn Qays? He is indeed oft-returning, forbearing. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not give him glad tidings? He said: Beware, do not let him hear lest you destroy him. Then he descended, and when we reached the mosque we found Buraydah al-Aslami at one of the doors of the mosque, and there was in the mosque a man prolonging prayer. Buraydah, who was given to jesting, said: O Mihjan, will you not pray as Sukbah prays? He did not reply anything to him and returned. When he came to his house he said: The best of our religion is its easiest, the best of your religion is its easiest, the best of your religion is its easiest, the best of your religion is its easiest - three times."
"18882","705 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated: Shuʿbah narrated from Abu Bishr from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Raja ibn Abi Raja from Mihjan ibn al-Adraʿ, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand. And he mentioned the like of it."
"18883","706 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuʿaythi narrated: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Mihjan ibn al-Adraʿ, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me for a need, then he met me while I was going out from the road of Madinah, so he took my hand and we went until we ascended to Uhud. Then he turned toward Madinah and said: Woe to it as a town; its people will leave it at its ripest. I said: O Prophet of Allah, who will eat its fruits? He said: The well-being of birds and beasts; and the Dajjal will not enter it. Whenever he intends to enter it, at every pass of its passes an angel with drawn sword will meet him. Then he turned until he was at the door of the mosque, and there was a man praying. He said: Does he say it truthfully? I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so, the most praying of the people of Madinah. He said: Do not let him hear lest you destroy him."
"18884","707 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated, (H) and Abu Khalifah narrated to us: Dawud ibn Shabib narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: Saʿid al-Jurayri informed us from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Mihjan ibn al-Adraʿ al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a barrier to the right of Madinah for a need. When I returned I went with him until he ascended Uhud and overlooked Madinah. He said: Woe to you as a town; your people will leave you while you are at your best. Then he descended and I descended with him until we came to the door of the mosque, and he saw a man praying. He placed his hand on my shoulder and illuminated him with his light, and said: Does he say it truthfully? He said it three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this one? And he is the most worshipping of the people of Madinah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear, do not let him hear lest you destroy him. He said it three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty is pleased with ease for this ummah and dislikes hardship for it. He said it three times."
"18885","One named Mirdas: Mirdas al-Aslami. 708 - Al-Husayn ibn Jaʿfar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated from Ismaʿil ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Mirdas al-Aslami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous will go as predecessors until none remains except dregs like the dregs of dates and barley; Allah will not care about them."
"18886","709 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid informed us from Bayan from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Mirdas al-Aslami, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The righteous will go as predecessors, and the righteous will be taken, the first then the first, until there remains dregs like the dregs of dates and barley; Allah will not care about them."
"18887","Mirdas ibn Urwah. 710 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Humayd narrated: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah from Mirdas ibn Urwah, he said: A man shot his brother and he fled, so we found him with Abu Bakr. So we went with him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he granted us retaliation from him."
"18888","One named Munqaʿ: Munqaʿ al-Taymi. 711 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi narrated; they claimed he means al-Munqaʿ ibn Tamim."
"18889","712 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismaʿil narrated, (H) and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Zakariya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to me: Sayf ibn Harun al-Burjumi narrated: Ismah ibn Bishr al-Burjumi narrated: al-Fazaʿ informed me - Sayf said: I think he witnessed al-Qadisiyyah - from al-Munqaʿ, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the charity of our camels, so he ordered it to be taken. I said: Among them are two she-camels as a gift for you, so I separated the gift from the charity. I stayed some days while the people discussed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send Khalid ibn al-Walid to the dependents of Egypt to take their charity. I said: By Allah, we have no wealth with our families nor their charity here. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on his she-camel, with him a black man whose head was level with the head of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I never saw anyone taller than him. When I drew near it was as if he leaned toward me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) restrained him. I said: The people have discussed such and such. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hand until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, and said: O Allah, I do not permit them to lie about me. Al-Munaqqaʿ said: So I did not narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except a hadith spoken by a Book or established by a Sunnah; he is lied about in his lifetime, so how after his death?"
"18890","Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad al-Fihri; Ismaʿil from Qays. 713 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Saʿid ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated, (H) and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated from Ismaʿil ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid al-Fihri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worldly life compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you placing his finger in the sea, so let him see with what it returns."
"18891","714 - Muʿadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated: Yahya narrated: Ismaʿil narrated: Qays narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Mustawrid saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and he pointed with his finger - : By Allah, the worldly life compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you placing his finger in the sea, then taking it out, so let him see with what it returns. And he gripped for me two joints of the forefinger."
"18892","715 - Al-Miqdad ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated: Marwan ibn Muʿawiyah narrated: Ibn Abi Khalid informed me from Qays from al-Mustawrid, brother of Banu Fihr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worldly life compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you placing his finger in this sea, so let him see with what it returns."
"18893","716 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Jarir narrated from Ismaʿil ibn Abi Khalid from Qays, he said: I heard al-Mustawrid saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and he pointed with his finger -: By Allah, the worldly life compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you placing his finger in the sea, then taking it out, so let him see with what it returns."
"18894","717 - Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah narrated: Muhammad ibn Saʿid ibn Sabiq narrated: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worldly life compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you walking to the sea and inserting his finger."
"18895","718 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Amr al-Wakiʿi narrated to us: Saʿid ibn Zunbur narrated: Ismaʿil ibn Mujalid narrated from Bayan and Ismaʿil ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The righteous will go, the first then the first, until there remains like the dregs of dates; Allah will not care about it."
"18896","719 - Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Subayh al-Zayyat al-Kufi narrated to us: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated: my father narrated: Sharik narrated from Ismaʿil ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous will go as predecessors."
"18897","720 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Amr ibn Awn narrated: Abu Bakr al-Dahiri narrated from Ismaʿil ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid al-Fihri, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with gout and complained to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The midday heats have belied you."
"18898","721 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Amr ibn Awn narrated: Abu Bakr al-Dahiri narrated from Ismaʿil ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid al-Fihri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return the needle and thread; whoever misappropriates a needle or thread will be burdened to bring it, and he will not bring it."
"18899","Mujalid ibn Saʿid from Qays from al-Mustawrid. 722 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Nuʿman narrated, (H) and Muʿadh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both said: Musaddad narrated, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Mujalid from Qays from al-Mustawrid - a man of Banu Fihr who had companionship - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the worldly life compared to the Hereafter is only like a man placing his finger in the sea, then it returns to him."
"18900","723 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim narrated, (H) and Muʿadh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both said: Musaddad narrated, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Mujalid from Qays from al-Mustawrid, he said: I was in the travelling party with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then his eye fell upon a discarded kid thrown away, so he said: Do you see this was worthless to its owners? They said: From its worthlessness they threw it away. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the worldly life is indeed more worthless to Allah than this is to its owners."
"18901","724 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated: Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated from Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad from Mujalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two: the forefinger and the middle finger."
"18902","Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr from al-Mustawrid. 725 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, both said: al-Qaʿnabi narrated: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated from al-Harith ibn Yazid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, he said: We were in a gathering in which were al-Mustawrid and Amr ibn Ghaylan ibn Salamah. So al-Mustawrid said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is in charge of a task for us and has no wife, let him take a wife; and whoever has no servant, let him take a servant; and whoever has no dwelling, let him take a dwelling; and whoever has no mount, let him take a mount. Abu Bakr said: You have said much, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acquires beyond that is a misappropriator."
"18903","726 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated: Ibn Hubayrah narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, he said: I was in a gathering in which were al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad and Amr ibn Ghaylan. So I heard al-Mustawrid saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is in charge of a task for us and has no wife, let him marry; or no servant, let him take a servant; or no dwelling, let him take a dwelling; or no mount, let him take a mount. So whoever acquires beyond that is a misappropriator or a thief."
"18904","727 - Jaʿfar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Musa ibn Marzuq al-Raqqi narrated: al-Muʿafa ibn Imran narrated: al-Awzaʿi narrated: al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is a worker for us, let him acquire a wife; and if he has no servant, let him acquire a servant; and whoever has no dwelling, let him acquire a dwelling."
"18905","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from al-Mustawrid. 728 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, (H) and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated, both said: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated: Yazid ibn Amr al-Maʿafiri narrated from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed ablution, run his little finger through the toes of his feet."
"18906","Hudayj ibn Amr from al-Mustawrid. 729 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated from al-Harith ibn Yazid from Hudayj ibn Amr, he said: I heard al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For every nation there is a term, and the term of the nation of Muhammad is one hundred years. He said: So when the hundred passes, what Allah promised it comes to it."
"18907","730 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Kamil ibn Talhah narrated: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Hudayj ibn Abi Amr, he said: I heard al-Mustawrid saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every nation has a term, and the term of my nation is one hundred years; so when one hundred years pass over my nation, what Allah promised it comes to it. Ibn Lahiʿah said: Meaning abundance of tribulations."
"18908","Abu Ishaq al-Sabiʿi from al-Mustawrid. 731 - Muttalib ibn Shuʿayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani from al-Mustawrid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the worldly life compared to the Hereafter is only like a man inserting his finger into the sea then taking it out; with what does it return?"
"18909","Amir al-Shaʿbi from al-Mustawrid. 732 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ismaʿil ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated: Hibban ibn Ali narrated from Mujalid from al-Shaʿbi from al-Mustawrid, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I was sent in the breath of the Hour, so I preceded it as this precedes; and he pointed with his two fingers, the forefinger and the middle finger."
"18910","733 - Saʿid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us: Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar narrated: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated: Bakr ibn Khunays narrated from Ashʿath ibn Sawwar from al-Shaʿbi from al-Mustawrid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worldly life has taken from the Hereafter only like a needle dipped in the sea takes of its water."
"18911","Waqqas ibn Rabiʿah from al-Mustawrid. 734 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Sulayman ibn Musa from Waqqas ibn Rabiʿah from al-Mustawrid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats by means of his brother a morsel, Allah will feed him a like morsel of it from the fire of Hell."
"18912","735 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Missisi and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated: Baqiyyah narrated from Ibn Thawban from his father from Makhul from Waqqas ibn Rabiʿah from al-Mustawrid, that he narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats by means of a Muslim man a morsel in this world, Allah will feed him the like of it in Hell; and whoever is clothed by means of a Muslim man with a garment, Allah will clothe him the like of it from Hell; and whoever stands with a Muslim in a station of showing off, Allah will place him in a station of reputation and showing off."
"18913","Abd al-Karim ibn al-Harith al-Misri from al-Mustawrid. 736 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us: my father narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated, (H) and Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated: my uncle Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated from Abd al-Karim ibn al-Harith, that al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Hour will come while the Romans are the most numerous of people. That reached Amr ibn al-As, so he said: What are these hadiths mentioned from you? So al-Mustawrid said to him: I said what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Amr said: If you said that, they are the most forbearing of people at tribulation, the most patient of people at calamity, and the best of people to their weak and poor."
"18914","Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi from al-Mustawrid. 737 - Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated: Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated: Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Musa ibn Ulayy from his father from al-Mustawrid al-Fihri, that he said to Amr ibn al-As: The Hour will come while the Romans are the most numerous of people. He said: Look at what you say? He said: I say only what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The righteous will go as predecessors, and there will remain dregs like the dregs of dates and barley; Allah will not care about them."
"18915","One named Mikhnaf: Mikhnaf ibn Sulaym al-Ghamidi. 738 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Nuʿman narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Ibn Awn from a man of the people of Kufah called Abu Ramlah from Mikhnaf ibn Sulaym, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Arafah and said: Upon every Muslim household is a sacrifice and an atirah. Do you know what the atirah is? The one you call al-Rajabiyyah."
"18916","739 - Muʿadh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muʿadh narrated to us: my father narrated, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Muʿadh narrated from Ibn Awn, he said: Abu Ramlah informed me from Mikhnaf ibn Sulaym, he said: We were standing with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O people, upon every household in every year is a sacrifice and an atirah. Do you know what the atirah is? It is what people call al-Rajabiyyah."
"18917","740 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Abd al-Karim informed me from Habib ibn Mikhnaf from his father, he said: I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah while he was saying: Do you know it? And I do not know what they replied to him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the people of every house is to slaughter a sheep in every Rajab, and in every sacrifice a sheep."
"18918","One named Muhayyisah: Muhayyisah ibn Masʿud al-Ansari. 741 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me: the freedman of Yazid ibn Thabit narrated to me: the daughter of Muhayyisah narrated to me from her father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you overcome of the men of the Jews, kill him. So Muhayyisah leapt upon Ibn Sunaynah - a man of the Jewish merchants who used to associate and trade with them - and killed him. Huwayyisah was then not yet Muslim and was older than Muhayyisah. When he killed him, Huwayyisah began striking him saying: O enemy of Allah, did you kill him? By Allah, how much fat is in your belly from his wealth! So I said: By Allah, if he had ordered me to kill you I would have struck your neck. He said: By Allah, that was indeed the beginning of the Islam of Huwayyisah. He said: By Allah, if Muhammad ordered you to kill me would you kill me? Muhayyisah said: Yes, by Allah. Huwayyisah said: By Allah, a religion that reaches this is indeed wondrous. So Huwayyisah accepted Islam."
"18919","742 - Muttalib ibn Shuʿayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated: al-Layth narrated to me: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated from Abu Ufayr al-Ansari from Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah from Muhayyisah ibn Masʿud al-Ansari, that he had a cupper slave called Nafiʿ Abu Taybah, so he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about his earnings. He said: Do not approach it. So he repeated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Feed with it the water-carrying camel; put it in its stomach."
"18920","743 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from al-Zuhri from Haram ibn Saʿidah from Muhayyisah ibn Masʿud from his father from his grandfather Muhayyisah, he said: I had a cupper slave called Abu Taybah, so he earned much earning. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earning of the cupper, he sought license from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he refused him. He kept speaking to him and mentioning need to him until he said to him: Throw his earning into the belly of your water-carrying camel."
"18921","744 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Salamah ibn Abi Kabshah narrated: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated: Rabiʿah ibn Salih narrated from al-Zuhri from Haram ibn Saʿd ibn Muhayyisah from his father from his grandfather, that he sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the earnings of the cupper, so he denied it to him. He kept returning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioning his need to him until he permitted him to feed his water-carrying camel and his slaves with it."
"18922","Mukhariq Abu Qabus. 745 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Wadaʿi al-Qadi narrated to us: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated: Sharik narrated from Simak from Qabus ibn Mukhariq from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No nation is sanctified in which the right of the weak is not taken without faltering."
"18923","746 - Muʿadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated from Simak ibn Harb from Qabus ibn Mukhariq from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man comes to me wanting my wealth? He said: Remind him of Allah. He said: And if he does not remember? He said: Then seek help against him from the Muslims around you. He said: And if there is no one around me? He said: Then seek help against him from the ruler. He said: And if the ruler forsakes me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fight for your wealth until you are among the martyrs of the Hereafter or you prevent that."
"18924","747 - Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us: Abu al-Rabiʿ al-Zahrani narrated: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated from Simak ibn Harb from Qabus ibn al-Mukhariq from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, if a man comes to me wanting my wealth, how do you command me? He said: Then remind him by Allah. I said: What if I do so and he does not desist? He said: You seek aid from the Muslims. I said: What if I do so and find none of the Muslims? He said: You seek aid from the ruler. I said: What if the ruler forsakes me and insists on seizing my wealth from me? He said: Then fight him until you protect your wealth or you are among the martyrs of the Hereafter."
"18925","748 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Tai narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Tai narrated: Ibn Simak ibn Harb narrated from his father, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What if a man meets me in an empty land wanting my wealth? He said: Remind him by Allah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, and if he does not remember? He said: Then seek help against him from those besides you of the Muslims. He said: And if there is no one around me? He said: Then seek help against him from the ruler. He said: What if the ruler refuses me? He said: Then fight for your wealth until you are among the martyrs of the Hereafter or you protect your wealth."
"18926","749 - Ismaʿil ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated: Musʿab ibn al-Miqdam al-Khathʿami narrated: Israil narrated from Simak ibn Harb from Qabus ibn al-Mukhariq from his father, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What if a man comes to me wanting to take my wealth? He said: Remind him by Allah. He said: What if I remind him by Allah and he does not remember? He said: Seek help against him from the ruler. He said: What if the ruler forsakes me? He said: Seek help from those Muslims in your presence. He said: What if none is present with me? He said: Then fight for your wealth, or you are killed and are among the martyrs of the Hereafter."
"18927","One named Murrah: Murrah ibn Kaʿb al-Sulami then al-Bahzi; and it was differed over his name, so it was said Kaʿb ibn Murrah, and the correct is Murrah ibn Kaʿb. 750 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated, (H) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, both said: Abu Hilal narrated from Qatadah from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Murrah al-Bahzi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A tribulation will agitate over the earth like the horns of cows. Then a veiled man passed, so he said: This one and his companions on that day are upon guidance - and it was Uthman ibn Affan."
"18928","751 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Nuʿman narrated: Khalid ibn al-Harith ibn Sulaym narrated: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq: Harim ibn al-Harith and Usamah ibn Khuraym narrated to us - and they used to contend over Murrah al-Bahzi - he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the road of Madinah, and he said: How will you act regarding a tribulation that will be in the regions of the earth as if it were the horns of cows? We said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall we act? And before him was a man, so he said: Follow this one and his companions. So I went to him while he was hastening, took the man and turned him toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This one, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: And he was Uthman ibn Affan."
"18929","752 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Abu Usamah narrated: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to me: Harim ibn al-Harith and Usamah ibn Khuraym narrated to me - and they used to contend - and they narrated to me a hadith while neither one perceived that his companion had narrated it to me - from Murrah al-Bahzi, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the road of Madinah, he said: How will you act with a tribulation that erupts in the regions of the earth as if it were the horns of cows? They said: What shall we do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon you is this one and his companions - and follow this one and his companions - and I hastened until I turned the man, and said: O Prophet of Allah, this one? He said: This one. And it was Uthman ibn Affan."
"18930","753 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated, (H) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, both said: Muʿawiyah ibn Salih narrated: Salim ibn Amir narrated to me from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, he said: We were encamped with Muʿawiyah after the killing of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them both. So Murrah ibn Kaʿb al-Bahzi stood and said: By Allah, were it not for something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would not have stood this standing. When Muʿawiyah heard the mention of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he seated the people. He said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting, Uthman passed, combed and generous, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A tribulation will emerge from under the feet - or from under the two feet - of this one, and whoever follows him on that day is upon guidance. So I stood until I took the shoulder of Uthman until I turned him toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: This one? He said: Yes, this one and whoever follows him on that day is upon guidance. Then Abdullah ibn Hawalah al-Ansari stood from near the pulpit and said: You are indeed the companion of this? He said: Yes. He said: By Allah, I was indeed present at that gathering, and had I known I had a confirmer in the army I would have been the first to speak of it."
"18931","754 - Husayn ibn Wahb al-Ursufi narrated to us: Zakariya ibn Nafiʿ al-Ursufi narrated: Abbad ibn Abbad al-Ramli narrated from Abu Zurʿah al-Saybani from Abu Zurʿah al-Waʿlani from Kurayb al-Sahuli, he said: Murrah al-Bahzi narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will remain a group of my nation upon the truth, dominant over those who oppose them, and they are like a dish among eaters until the command of Allah comes while they are thus. We said: O Messenger of Allah, and where are they? He said: In the surroundings of Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: And he narrated to me that al-Ramlah is al-Rabwah, because it faces west and east."
"18932","755 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated: Shuʿbah narrated from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Jaʿd narrating from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt from Kaʿb ibn Murrah, or Murrah ibn Kaʿb, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against Mudar. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has given you and answered you, and your people have perished, so supplicate for them that He give them drink. He said: O Allah, give us a rescuing rain, wholesome, swift, abundant, enveloping, immediate, not delayed, beneficial not harmful. He said: Not a Friday or so passed until we were rained upon."
"18933","So it was said to Murrah ibn Kaʿb: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may your father be for Allah, and be cautious. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant frees a Muslim slave but it is his ransom from the Fire; requited, for every bone of its bones a bone of his bones; and any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women but they are his ransom from the Fire, requited, for every two bones of their bones a bone of his bones; and any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, she is her ransom from the Fire, requited, for every bone of her bones a bone of her bones."
"18934","756 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated: Shuʿbah narrated: Amr ibn Murrah, Mansur ibn al-Muʿtamir and Qatadah informed me from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaʿd, narrating from Ibn al-Simt, he said: I said to Kaʿb ibn Murrah, or Murrah ibn Kaʿb al-Sulami - Shuʿbah doubted -: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may your father be for Allah, and be cautious. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against Mudar, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has given you, answered you and aided you, and your people have perished, so supplicate Allah for them to give them drink. He said: O Allah, give us a rescuing rain, wholesome, fruitful, abundant, enveloping, immediate not delayed, beneficial not harmful. He said: Not a Friday passed over us until we were rained upon."
"18935","So I said: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may your father be for Allah, and be cautious. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim servant frees a Muslim man but he is his ransom from the Fire; requited, for every bone of his bones a bone of his bones; and no Muslim servant frees two Muslim women but they are his ransom from the Fire; requited, every two bones of their bones a bone of his bones; and no Muslim woman frees a Muslim woman but she is her ransom from the Fire; requited, every bone of her bones a bone of her bones from the Fire."
"18936","757 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaʿd from a man of the people of Sham from Murrah ibn Kaʿb ibn Murrah al-Bahzi, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which night is most heard? He said: The last depth of the night; then prayer is accepted until dawn rises, then no prayer until the sun is a spear or two spears high, then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands the standing of a spear, then no prayer until the sun declines, then prayer is accepted until the sun is a spear or two spears-length away, then no prayer until the sun sets."
"18937","Murrah al-Fihri, and he is Murrah ibn Amr ibn Habib ibn Wathilah ibn Amr ibn Shayban ibn Muharib ibn Fihr; he accepted Islam on the day of the Conquest. 758 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated, (H) Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us: Saʿid ibn Mansur narrated, both said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated from Safwan ibn Sulaym from a woman called Unaysah from Umm Saʿd bint Murrah al-Fihri from her father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and the guardian of the orphan, for him or for another, in Paradise like these two - and Sufyan pointed with his two fingers."
"18938","759 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Juhadah from Muhammad ibn Ajlan from a daughter of Murrah from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guardian of the orphan, for him or for another, when he is God-fearing, is with me in Paradise like these two - meaning the forefinger and the middle finger."
"18939","One named Muʿtamir: Muʿtamir Abu Hanash. 760 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated: Salih ibn Umar al-Wasiti narrated from Ismaʿil from Hanash ibn al-Muʿtamir from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying over a funeral, then a woman came with a censer intending the funeral, so he shouted at her until she entered into the thickets of Madinah."
"18940","One named Makhrafah: Makhrafah al-Abdi. 761 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muʿalla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated: Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated from Simak ibn Harb from Makhrafah al-Abdi, he said: We went out with merchant people selling cloth, with them a weigher weighing for hire. So we came to Makkah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought trousers from them, and said to the weigher: Weigh and give extra."
"18941","One named Mishrah: Mishrah Abu Mil. 762 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us: Yunus ibn Musa al-Sami and Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated, both said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated: Ubaydullah ibn Salamah ibn Wahram narrated to me from Mil bint Mishrah, she said: I saw my father trim his nails, then bury them, and say: O my daughter, thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"18942","One named Mukhawwal: Mukhawwal al-Sulami then al-Bahzi. 763 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki and Yahya ibn Musa al-Lakhmi narrated, (H) and Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us: Yunus ibn Musa al-Sami narrated, all said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul al-Makhzumi narrated in Makkah: al-Qasim ibn Mukhawwal al-Bahzi then al-Sulami narrated: I heard my father narrating - and he had reached Jahiliyyah and Islam - he said: I set my snares at al-Abwa, and a gazelle fell into one of my ropes, then the rope turned, so we went out on its trail following it. I found a man who had taken it, so we disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We found him alighting at Abwa under a tree, shaded by a leather mat, so he judged it between us in two halves. I said: O Messenger of Allah, these are my snares on its leg. He said: It is that. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are at water, and thirsty camels come to us, so we give them water from the water; is there reward for us in that? He said: Yes, in every moist liver there is reward. I said: O Messenger of Allah, tall camels with tied udders meet us while we are hungry. He said: Say: O owner of the camels, O owner of the camels - three times - and if he comes, otherwise untie its tying, then milk and drink, return its tying, and leave for the milk its inviters. Then he began narrating to us, saying: There will come upon people a time when the best wealth therein is sheep between the two mosques - meaning the mosque of Madinah and the mosque of Makkah - eating trees and coming to waters; its owner eats of its offspring and wears of its wools - or he said: of its hairs - while tribulations tremble among the roots of the Arabs, and blood is shed. He said it three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Fear Allah, establish prayer, give zakah, perform hajj of the House and umrah, be kind to your parents, join your kin, honor the guest, command good, forbid evil, and incline with the truth wherever it inclines. And the wording is of the hadith of Yunus ibn Musa."
"18943","One named Mujashiʿ: Mujashiʿ ibn Masʿud al-Sulami. 764 - Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Shibami narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: al-Thawri informed us from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father, he said: We were in a raid, and with us was a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Mujashiʿ of Banu Sulaym. Sheep became dear, so he ordered a caller who called: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A jadhaʿah suffices for what a thaniyyah suffices."
"18944","765 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Nuʿman narrated: Yazid ibn Zurayʿ narrated: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Mujashiʿ ibn Masʿud al-Sulami, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my brother Mujalid ibn Masʿud, so pledge him upon hijrah. He said: No hijrah after the conquest of Makkah, but I pledge him upon Islam."
"18945","766 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Jaʿfar al-Nufayli narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated, both said: Zuhayr ibn Muʿawiyah narrated: Asim al-Ahwal narrated from Abu Uthman: Mujashiʿ narrated to me, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my brother Maʿbad to pledge him upon hijrah. He said: The people of hijrah have gone with what is in it. I said: Upon what do you pledge him? He said: I pledge him upon Islam - or faith - and jihad. Then I met Maʿbad after, and asked him - and he was the elder of them - and he said: He spoke truth."
"18946","767 - Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Saʿd al-Dashtaki narrated: my father narrated: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated from Asim from Uthman from Mujashiʿ ibn Masʿud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"18947","768 - Jaʿfar ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi narrated to us: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated: Shayban narrated, (H) and al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abi Yaʿqub al-Kirmani narrated: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated: Shayban narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq informed me from Mujashiʿ ibn Masʿud, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge him upon hijrah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, rather we pledge upon Islam, for there is no hijrah after the Conquest, so you are of the followers in goodness."
"18948","One named Mujalid: Mujalid ibn Masʿud al-Sulami. 769 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Nuʿman narrated: Yazid ibn Zurayʿ narrated: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Mujashiʿ al-Sulami, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my brother Mujalid ibn Masʿud, so pledge him upon hijrah. He said: No hijrah after the conquest of Makkah, but I pledge him upon Islam."
"18949","One named Muharrish: Muharrish al-Kaʿbi. 770 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us: Saʿid ibn Abi Maryam narrated: Nafiʿ ibn Yazid informed me: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim informed me from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah from Muharrish al-Kaʿbi, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the night he left al-Jiʿranah until evening as one performing umrah, entered Makkah by night and completed his umrah, then went out under its night and reached al-Jiʿranah by morning as one who spent the night, until when the sun declined he went out from al-Jiʿranah in the belly of Sarif until the road joined the road of Madinah at Sarif. Muharrish said: So his umrah was hidden from many people for that."
"18950","771 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Muzahim ibn Zufar from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah from Muharrish al-Kaʿbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed umrah from al-Jiʿranah, then returned as one who spent the night, so his umrah was hidden from many people for that."
"18951","772 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated: Sufyan narrated: Ismaʿil ibn Umayyah narrated from Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid from Muharrish, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed umrah from al-Jiʿranah, and I looked at his back as if it were an ingot of silver, and he reached morning as one who spent the night."
"18952","One named Marthad: Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, ally of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib; a Badri martyred on the day of al-Rajiʿ. 773 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated from Abu al-Aswad from Urwah, in the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi."
"18953","774 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated from Abu al-Aswad from Urwah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, ally of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, to a clan of Hudhayl, and there were killed of the Muslims, then of Banu Hashim: Marthad ibn Abi Marthad."
"18954","775 - Abu Shuʿayb al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Jaʿfar al-Nufayli narrated: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to me, he said: A group of Adal and al-Qarah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Uhud and said: O Messenger of Allah, there is Islam among us, so send with us men of your companions to instruct us in religion, teach us the Quran, and teach us the laws of Islam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent six men of his companions: Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi - ally of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib - and he mentioned the story. He said: As for Marthad ibn Abi Marthad, Khalid ibn al-Bukayr, and Asim ibn Thabit, they said: By Allah, we will never accept a covenant nor contract from a polytheist ever, so they fought them until they killed them."
"18955","776 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated from Musa ibn Uqbah from Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those killed on the day of al-Rajiʿ: Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi."
"18956","What Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi narrated. 777 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: my uncle al-Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Yahya ibn Yaʿla narrated, (H) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated: Ismaʿil ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated: Yahya ibn Yaʿla al-Aslami narrated from Abdullah ibn Musa from al-Qasim al-Shami from Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi - and he was a Badri - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it pleases you that your prayer be accepted, let the best of you lead you, for they are your delegation between you and your Lord."
"18957","778 - Ahmad ibn al-Muʿalla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated: al-Walid ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Saib narrated from Abu Awn from Abu Idris from Marthad - and he was of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: Allah drew two lines in His Book, then lifted the Pen and wrote in one of them creation, and wrote in the other what creation will do."
"18958","One named Muhajir: Muhajir ibn Qunfudh al-Taymi, and Qunfudh is called drinker of gold; Qunfudh ibn Umayr ibn Judʿan ibn Amr ibn Kaʿb ibn Saʿd ibn Taym ibn Murrah ibn Kaʿb ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib. 779 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, (H) and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: Humayd and others informed us from al-Hasan from al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was urinating - or he said: I passed by him while he had urinated - so I greeted him, and he did not reply to me until he finished his ablution, then he replied to me."
"18959","780 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me: Muʿadh ibn Hisham narrated: my father narrated to me from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Hudayn ibn al-Mundhir Abu Sasan from al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, that he greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was urinating, so he did not reply to him until he performed ablution."
"18960","781 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn Talib narrated: Yazid ibn Zurayʿ narrated: Saʿid ibn Abi Arubah narrated from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Hudayn ibn al-Mundhir from Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, he said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and greeted while he was performing ablution, so I greeted him and he did not reply to me. When he finished he replied to me and excused himself to me, saying: Nothing prevented me from replying to you except that I disliked mentioning Allah while not in purity."
"18961","782 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated: Abu Muʿawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated from Ismaʿil ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw three upon a mount and said: The third is cursed."
"18962","Muhajir, freedman of Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 783 - Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Bukayr narrated: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to me, he said: I heard Bukayr saying: I heard Muhajir, freedman of Umm Salamah, saying: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for years, and he never said to me for something I did: Why did you do it? Nor for something I left: Why did you leave it? Ibn Bukayr said: This Bukayr in the hadith is my grandfather."
"18963","One named Masʿud: Masʿud, freedman of Farwah al-Aslami. 784 - Abdan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Saʿid al-Qattan narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated: Aflah ibn Saʿid narrated to me: Buraydah ibn Sufyan al-Aslami narrated to me from Masʿud - slave of his grandfather Farwah Abu Tamim - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr passed by me, so Abu Bakr said to me: O Masʿud, go to Abu Tamim your master and tell him to send with us a guide to take us by the most hidden road, and a camel and provisions. So I came to my master and told him, so he sent me and sent with me a camel and a waterskin of milk. So I came to them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood praying, with Abu Bakr on his right - so I stood behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pushed the chest of Abu Bakr, so we stood behind him."
"18964","Masʿud ibn al-Dahhak al-Lakhmi. 785 - Abu Masʿud Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: al-Muthanna narrated to me from his father Mutaʿ from his father Isa from his father Mutaʿ from his father Ziyad from his grandfather Masʿud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Mutaʿ and said to him: O Mutaʿ, you are obeyed among your people. And he said to him: Go to your companions, and carried him on a piebald horse, gave him the banner, and said: Whoever enters under this banner of mine is safe from punishment."
"18965","Masʿud Abu Muhammad al-Ansari then al-Khazraji; a Badri. 786 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated: Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, in the naming of those who witnessed Badr of the Ansar, then of Banu al-Khazraj, then of Banu al-Najjar: Abu Muhammad al-Ansari, and his name is Masʿud ibn Aws ibn Asram ibn Zayd ibn Thaʿlabah ibn Ghanm ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar."
"18966","787 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Saʿid ibn Abi Maryam narrated: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated: Yazid ibn Amr al-Maʿafiri narrated to me from a freedman of Rufayʿ ibn Thabit, that a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a Berber slave-girl for two hundred dinars, so he sent her to Abu Muhammad al-Badri - of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was a Badri - and he gave him the Berber slave-girl. When she came to him he said: These are of the Magians whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, and those who associated partners. So I narrated this hadith to a man, and he narrated to me that Yahya ibn Saʿid narrated to him that an uncle of his died in the Maghrib and he was a Badri."
"18967","Masʿud ibn Saʿd ibn Khalid al-Ansari then al-Zuraqi; martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 788 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated: Ibn Lahiʿah narrated from Abu al-Aswad from Urwah, in the naming of those martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the Ansar, then of Banu Zurayq: Masʿud ibn Saʿd ibn Khalid."
"18968","789 - Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated from Musa ibn Uqbah from Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the Ansar, then of Banu Zurayq: Masʿud ibn Saʿd ibn Qays."
"18969","Masʿud ibn Amr. 790 - Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Humayd ibn Masʿadah narrated: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated: Ibn Abi Layla narrated from Abd al-Karim from Saʿid ibn Yazid from Masʿud ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The servant will keep asking while rich until he scrapes his face, so he has no face with Allah."
"18970","Masʿud ibn al-Aswad al-Adawi, and he is Masʿud ibn al-Aswad ibn Harithah ibn Nadlah ibn Awf ibn Ubayd ibn Uwayj ibn Adi ibn Kaʿb; his mother is al-Ajma bint Amir. 791 - Muttalib ibn Shuʿayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated: al-Layth narrated to me, (H) and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated: Layth ibn Saʿd narrated: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah, that his maternal aunt, the daughter of Masʿud ibn al-Ajma, narrated to him, that her father said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the Makhzumiyyah who stole a velvet garment: We ransom her with forty ounces. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purification is better for her. And he ordered her, so her hand was cut."
"18971","792 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah from his mother Aishah bint Masʿud ibn al-Aswad from her father, he said: When the woman stole the velvet garment I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we deemed that grave, and she was of Quraysh. So we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke to him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, we ransom her with forty ounces. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purification is better for her. When we heard the soft speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we went to Usamah ibn Zayd and spoke to him, saying: Intercede for us with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the affair of this woman, and we ransom her with forty ounces. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he stood among us as a preacher and said: O people, why do you speak much about a hadd of Allah that fell upon a maidservant of Allah? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, had Fatimah bint Muhammad committed what this one committed, I would have cut her hand. So the people despaired and her hand was cut."
"18972","793 - Abu Zurʿah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, both said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated: my father narrated, all of them from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah from his mother Aishah bint Masʿud ibn al-Aswad from her father Masʿud, he said: When the woman stole that velvet garment from the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered its cutting, we deemed that grave, and she was a woman of Quraysh. So we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke to him, saying: We ransom her with forty ounces. He said: Purification is better for her. When we heard the soft speech of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we came to Usamah ibn Zayd and said to him: Speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the affair of this woman, and we ransom her with forty ounces. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he stood as a preacher and said: O people, why do you speak much to me about a hadd of Allah that fell upon a maidservant of Allah? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, had Fatimah bint the Messenger of Allah committed what this woman committed, I would have established the hadd upon her."
"18973","Masʿud ibn Khalid al-Khuzaʿi. 794 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us: Abu Malik ibn Abi Farah al-Khuzaʿi narrated: my father Abu Farah narrated to me from his father al-Walid from his grandfather Masʿud ibn Khalid, he said: I sent a sheep to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then went for a need, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned half of it to them. So I returned to Umm Khunas - his wife - and there was meat with her. I said: O Umm Khunas, what is this meat? She said: This meat your friend returned to us from the sheep you sent to him. He said: Why do you not feed your dependents since morning? She said: These are their leftovers, and I have fed all of them; and they used to slaughter two and three sheep and they did not suffice them."
"18974","One named Masruq: Masruq ibn Wail al-Hadrami. 795 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Hadhdha narrated: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated from Utbah ibn Abi Utbah from Sulayman ibn Amr from al-Dahhak ibn al-Nuʿman ibn Saʿd, that Masruq ibn Wail came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah at al-Aqiq, accepted Islam and his Islam was good. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I love that you send to my people a man to call them to Islam, and that you write for us a letter to my people; perhaps Allah will guide them by it. So he said to Muʿawiyah: Write for him: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate; to the Afnad of Hadramawt: establishing prayer, giving zakah, charity upon capacity, the taymah in pastured animals a fifth, in rain-watered a tenth; no khilat, no wirat, no shighar, no shinaq, no janab, no jalab; and two camels are not joined in one rope; whoever sells fruit before safety from blight has dealt in usury; and every intoxicant is forbidden. And he sent to them Ziyad ibn Labid al-Ansari. As for khilat: livestock is not combined; as for wirat: it is not valued by price; as for shighar: a man marries his daughter and the other marries him his daughter without dowry; al-shinaq: that he hobbles her in her resting places; al-ijba: that the fruit be sold before it is safe from blight."
"18975","One named Mikhmar: Mikhmar ibn Haydah al-Qushayri. 796 - Ahmad ibn al-Muʿalla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated: Ismaʿil ibn Ayyash narrated: Sulayman ibn Sulaym al-Kinani narrated from Hakim ibn Muʿawiyah from his uncle Mikhmar ibn Haydah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No bad omen, and blessing may be in three: in the woman, the horse, and the house."
"18976","797 - Abu Zurʿah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated: Saʿid ibn Bashir narrated from Qatadah from Hakim ibn Muʿawiyah from his uncle Mikhmar ibn Haydah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am absent a month from water while my family is with me, so I approach them? He said: Yes. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am absent months. He said: Even if you are absent thirty years."
"18977","One named Mazin: Mazin ibn al-Ghadubah al-Azdi. 798 - Muhammad ibn Asim al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated: Husayn ibn Kathir narrated: my grandfather Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Najdah al-Himsi from al-Awzaʿi from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from his father Salih ibn al-Mutawakkil, he said: I heard Mazin ibn al-Ghadubah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Upon you is truthfulness, for it guides to Paradise."
"18978","799 - Musa ibn Jumhur al-Tinnisi al-Simsar narrated to us: Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated: Hisham ibn Muhammad ibn al-Saib al-Kalbi narrated from his father from Abdullah al-Umani from Mazin ibn al-Ghadubah, he said: I used to tend an idol called Bahar at Sama il - a village in Oman - and we sacrificed one day at it an atirah - which is the slaughtered animal - and I heard a voice from the idol saying: O Mazin, hear and rejoice; good has appeared and evil is hidden; a Prophet is sent from Mudar with the religion of Allah the Great, the Great; so leave a hewn one of stone, you are saved from Saqar. He said: I was frightened at that and said: This is indeed wondrous. Then after some days I sacrificed an atirah and heard a voice from the idol saying: Come to me, come; hear what you are not ignorant of: this is a sent Prophet who came with revealed truth, so believe in him that you be just, from the heat of a kindled fire whose fuel is stones. So I said: This is indeed wondrous, and it is good intended for me. While we were thus, a man from Hijaz arrived. We said: What news behind you? He said: A man appeared called Ahmad, saying to whoever comes to him: Answer the caller of Allah. I said: This is the news of what I heard. So I went to the idol and broke it into pieces, rode my mount, and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He explained Islam to me and I accepted Islam, and I said: ... He said - meaning Amr ibn al-Salt and his brothers, Banu Khutamah - Mazin said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man fond of music, wine-drinking and immoral women, and hard years pressed upon us, removing wealth and emaciating offspring and dependents, and I have no child; so supplicate Allah to remove from me what I find, grant us modesty, and give me a child. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, replace for him music with recitation of the Quran, the forbidden with the lawful, immorality with chastity of the private part, wine with drink in which there is no sin, grant him modesty, and give him a child. Mazin said: So Allah removed from me what I found, granted us modesty, I learned half the Quran, Oman became fertile, I performed many pilgrimages, and Allah gave me Hayyan ibn Mazin. And I began saying verses. When I came to my people they blamed and reviled me, ordered their poet who lampooned me. I said: If I answer him, satire is only for myself. So I withdrew from them to the seashore and said verses, and a great company of them came to me saying: O son of uncle, we faulted an affair in you and disliked it for you; if you refuse, your affair and religion. Return and manage our affairs. So I was the manager of their affairs, and returned with them, then Allah guided them after to Islam."
"18979","Mazin ibn Khaythamah and Hubayl al-Sakuniyyan. 800 - Abu Zurʿah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafiʿ narrated: Ismaʿil ibn Ayyash narrated from Safwan ibn Amr from Amr ibn Qays ibn Thawr ibn Mazin, that his grandfather Mazin ibn Khaythamah and Hubayl ibn Kaʿb - one of Banu Mazin - Muʿadh ibn Jabal sent them both on the day he alighted among al-Sakun and al-Sakasik, and he fought until the people accepted Islam coming as delegations to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he made brotherhood between al-Sakun and al-Sakasik."
"18980","One named Maʿbad: Maʿbad al-Judhami. 801 - Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Tawwazi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Bajali Sajjadah narrated: Yahya ibn Saʿid al-Umawi narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Humayd ibn Mazin from Naʿjah ibn Zayd al-Judhami from his father, he said: Rifaʿah ibn Zayd al-Judhami came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he wrote for him a letter in it: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate; this is a letter from Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, to Rifaʿah ibn Zayd: I sent him to his people generally and whoever enters among them, calling them to Allah and His Messenger. Whoever believes is in the party of Allah and the party of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and whoever turns away has safety for two months. When he came to his people they answered him. Then he went until he alighted at al-Harrah - Harrah al-Rajla - then soon Dihyah al-Kalbi approached from Qurayzah when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him, until he was at a valley of their valleys called Shinan - with him trade of his, al-Hunayd ibn Uways and his father al-Uways al-Dubaʿi - a branch of Judham - attacked him and took all he had. Then a group of the people of Rifaʿah rose to him; al-Nuʿman ibn Abi Jiʿal came to him among those who came until they met them and fought. Qurrah ibn Ashqar al-Dalaʿi threw a stone at al-Nuʿman ibn Abi Jiʿal and hit his ankle and bloodied it, saying: I am Ibn Uthalah. Then al-Nuʿman ibn Abi Jiʿal shot him with an arrow and hit his knee, saying: I am Ibn Iqalah. Hassan ibn Millah al-Dabbi had accompanied Dihyah al-Kalbi before that, taught him Umm al-Kitab, and they rescued what was in their hands and returned it to Dihyah. Then Dihyah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him their news, and sought from him the blood of al-Hunayd and his father Uways; and that is what stirred Zayd and Judham. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Zayd ibn Harithah with an army. Ghatafan, Judham, Wail, and whoever was of Salman and Saʿd ibn Hudhayl had turned when Rifaʿah came to them with the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he alighted at al-Harrah - Harrah al-Rajla - with Rifaʿah at Kuraʿ al-Ghamim, with him a horseman of Banu al-Dubayb, and the rest of Banu al-Dubayb at Wadi Madariq on the side of al-Harrah."
"18981","Maʿbad ibn Hawdhah al-Ansari. 802 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuʿaym narrated: Ali ibn Thabit narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Nuʿman ibn Maʿbad ibn Hawdhah al-Ansari from his father from his grandfather - raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) -: He commanded the use of antimony with musk at sleep, saying: Let the fasting one beware it."
"18982","Maʿbad al-Qurashi. 803 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from Abd al-Razzaq from Israil from Simak ibn Harb from Maʿbad al-Qurashi, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Qudayd, and a man came to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you eat anything today for the day of Ashura? He said: No, except I drank water. He said: Then eat nothing until the sun sets, and command those behind you to fast this day."
"18983","One named Madluk: Madluk Abu Sufyan. 804 - Jaʿfar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi and Abu Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, both said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated: Matar ibn al-Ala narrated to me: my paternal aunt Aminah bint Abi al-Shaʿtha and Qutbah her freedwoman narrated to me that they saw Madluk Abu Sufyan and heard him saying: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my freedmen and accepted Islam. Aminah said: So I saw what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped of his head black, while what besides that had whitened."
"18984","One named Munib: Munib al-Azdi. 805 - Jaʿfar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated: Utbah ibn Hammad narrated: Munib ibn Mudrik ibn Munib al-Azdi narrated from his father from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Jahiliyyah while he was saying to people: Say: There is no god but Allah, you prosper. Some spat in his face, some threw dust on him, some reviled him, until midday. Then a girl came with a cup of water and washed his face - or his hands - and said: O my daughter, do not fear poverty nor humiliation upon your father. I said: Who is this? They said: Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a radiant young girl."
"18985","One named Mudrikah: Mudrikah ibn al-Harith al-Azdi. 806 - Jaʿfar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Hisham ibn Khalid narrated: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ismaʿil ibn Abdullah narrated from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi from Mudrikah ibn al-Harith, he said: I performed hajj with my father, and when we were at Mina there was a crowd. I said to my father: What is this crowd? He said: Over this Sabian. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you prosper."
"18986","One named Matar: Matar ibn Ukamis, and it is said Ukabis; his companionship was differed over. 807 - Abdullah ibn Saʿid ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, (H) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated... both said: Abu Utbah al-Azraq Abbad ibn Musa narrated, both said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Abu Ishaq from Matar ibn Ukamis, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty decrees for a man to die in a land, He makes for him therein a need."
"18987","808 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated: Israil narrated from Abu Ishaq from Matar ibn Ukamis, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty decrees the death of a servant in a land, He makes for him therein a need."
"18988","One named Maʿiz: Maʿiz al-Tamimi. 809 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated: Shuʿbah narrated from Abu Musa from Abu Masʿud al-Jurayri from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Maʿiz, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah alone, then jihad, then an accepted hajj surpassing other deeds as between sunrise and sunset."
"18989","810 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to me: Khalid informed us from al-Jurayri from Hayyan ibn Umayr from Maʿiz, he said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah, and jihad in His path. Then he trembled, then said: Mah? He said: Then a deed better than other deeds except like an accepted hajj."
"18990","811 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuʿi al-Qadi narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated: Saʿid al-Jurayri narrated from Hayyan ibn Umayr: Maʿiz narrated: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah, and jihad in His path. Then the thigh of the questioner trembled, so he said: Then Mah? He said: Then a deed better than other deeds except like an accepted hajj."
"18991","One named Mazidah: Mazidah, grandfather of Hud, al-Asari, and it is said al-Abdi. 812 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated: Talib ibn Hujayr al-Abdi narrated: Hud al-Asari narrated to me from his grandfather, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was narrating to his companions, he said to them: There will appear to you from this direction a mounted party, the best people of the East. So Umar ibn al-Khattab stood going toward that direction and met thirteen riders. He welcomed and drew near, saying: Who are the people? They said: Men of Abd al-Qays. He said: What brought you to this land, trade? They said: No. He said: Will you sell these swords of yours? They said: No. He said: Perhaps you came seeking this man? They said: Yes. So he walked narrating to them until he looked at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This is your companion whom you seek. So the people threw themselves from their mounts; some hastened, some hurried, some walked until they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), took his hand and kissed it, and sat to him. Ashajj remained - the youngest of the people - so he kneeled the camels, hobbled them, gathered the baggage of the people, then came walking gently until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), took his hand and kissed it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: In you are two traits Allah and His Messenger love. He said: What are they, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Forbearance and deliberation. He said: O Prophet of Allah, a nature I was fashioned upon, or a character from me? He said: Rather a nature you were fashioned upon. He said: Praise be to Allah who fashioned me upon what Allah and His Messenger love. The people turned to dates of theirs eating them, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began telling them of them, naming for them: this is such, and this is such. They said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah, we are not more knowing of their names than you. He said: Yes. They said to a man of them: Feed us from the remainder of the bow that remained of your bag. So he brought them al-Burni. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is al-Burni; it is of the best of your dates, a cure with no disease in it."
"18992","813 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated: Talib ibn Hujayr narrated: Hud al-Asari narrated from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the Conquest with gold and silver upon his sword."
"18993","814 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated: Yahya ibn Rashid narrated: Abu Bakr Talib ibn Hujayr narrated: Hud al-Asari narrated: I heard my grandfather Mazidah al-Abdi saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tied the banners of the Ansar and made them yellow."
"18994","One named Musayyab: Musayyab ibn Hazn ibn Abi Wahb ibn Amr ibn Aidh ibn Imran ibn Makhzum; his mother is Umm al-Harith bint Shuʿbah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Qays ibn Abd Wudd ibn Nasr ibn Malik ibn Hasal; and he is the father of Saʿid ibn al-Musayyab, and he was of those who pledged under the tree. 815 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated: Sufyan narrated from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I said to Saʿid ibn al-Musayyab: Where is the mosque of the tree? So he laughed and said: We do not know. Then he said: My father informed me that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that year and that they were made to forget it."
"18995","816 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Saʿid ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated: Israil narrated from Tariq ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I went out performing hajj and passed by people praying at a mosque saying: This is the tree of the pledge of Ridwan when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledged. So I came to Saʿid ibn al-Musayyab and informed him, and he said: My father narrated to me that he was among those who pledged the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under the tree. He said: When we went out the next year we forgot it and could not find it. Saʿid said: If the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not know it and you know it, then you are more knowing."
"18996","817 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Shabbah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from his father who said: I saw the tree, then I came to it afterwards and did not recognize it."
"18997","818 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ubayd ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from his father, that his father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: What is your name? I said: Hazn. He said: You are Sahl. He said: I will not abandon a name. Sa'id said: That roughness has remained among us until now."
"18998","819 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his grandfather: What is your name? He said: Hazn. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather you are Sahl. He said: I will not change a name my father gave me. That roughness has continued among us ever since."
"18999","820 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Ya'la al-Tawwazi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from his father who said: When death came to Abu Talib, with Abu Jahl ibn Hisham and Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayyah present with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and said: O uncle, say: There is no god but Allah, a word with which I will argue for you before Allah. They said: O Abu Talib, do you turn away from the religion of Abd al-Muttalib? Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Indeed you do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills, and He knows best those who are guided."
"19000","Those named Mu'ayqib. Mu'ayqib ibn Abi Fatimah al-Dawsi, among the emigrants to Abyssinia, an ally of Banu Sa'id ibn al-As the elder, and he was in charge of the treasury for Umar ibn al-Khattab. 821 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated that to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"19001","What Mu'ayqib transmitted. 822 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us; (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Mu'ayqib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"19002","823 - Abd Allah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Mu'ayqib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"19003","824 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah and Abu Zayd al-Hawtiyyan both said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah who said: Mu'ayqib narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you must do it, then once; meaning wiping the pebbles."
"19004","825 - Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, Mu'ayqib narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding a man who levels the pebbles and dust where he prostrates: If you must do it, then once."
"19005","826 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Mu'ayqib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wipe while you are praying, and if you must do it, then once, leveling the pebbles."
"19006","827 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Mu'ayqib, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wiping in prayer, and he said: Once, otherwise leave it."
"19007","828 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Mu'ayqib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him about wiping in prayer: If you must do it, then once."
"19008","829 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Muharibi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from his father, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Abu Abd Allah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Mu'ayqib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Throne shook at the death of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh."
"19009","830 - Al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Yunus al-Ahwazi the scribe narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Yazid al-Nahratiri narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mu'ayqib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed i'tikaf in a dome of palm leaves, its door made of mat, with the people in the mosque."
"19010","831 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, they said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Abu Makin Nuh ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, Iyas ibn al-Harith ibn Mu'ayqib narrated to me, from his grandfather Mu'ayqib, who said: The ring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of iron twisted with silver, and it was sometimes in my hand. And Mu'ayqib was in charge of the seal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19011","832 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to me, Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Mu'ayqib, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Fire is forbidden for the gentle, lenient, easy, approachable one."
"19012","Those named Maysarah. Maysarah al-Fajr al-Uqayli. 833 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awaqi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Maysarah al-Fajr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you a prophet? He said: While Adam was between the spirit and the body."
"19013","834 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Mansur ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah al-Uqayli, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Maysarah al-Fajr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you a prophet? He said: While Adam was between the spirit and the body."
"19014","Those named Maymun. Maymun ibn Sinbadh. 835 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Harun ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, who said: I heard a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Maymun ibn Sinbadh say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The uprightness of my ummah is by its worst ones."
"19015","Those named Mihran. Mihran, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); there is disagreement about his name, they said: Kaysan or Hurmuz, and in my view the correct one is Mihran, because al-Thawri is the most precise of those who transmitted it. 836 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, Umm Kulthum bint Ali narrated to me - and I had come to her with charity he had ordered - and she said: Beware of our youths, for Maymun or Mihran, freedman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed me that he passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: O Maymun - or O Mihran - we are a household forbidden charity, and our freedmen are from ourselves, so do not eat charity."
"19016","837 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib who said: I entered upon Umm Kulthum bint Ali with something of charity and she said: A freedman of ours called Kaysan - or Hurmuz - informed me that he passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: So he called me and I came, and he said: O so-and-so, we are a household forbidden to take charity, and the freedman of a people is from themselves, so do not eat charity."
"19017","Those named Munaydhir. Munaydhir al-Aslami. 838 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Hayy ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from al-Munaydhir, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he used to be in Ifriqiyah - who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says in the morning: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet, I am the guarantor, I will take him by the hand until I admit him to Paradise."
"19018","Those named Mundhir. Mundhir ibn Sawa, governor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over Bahrain. 839 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Idris al-Hulwani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to al-Mundhir ibn Sawa: Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qibla, and eats our slaughtered meat, that is the Muslim, with the protection of Allah and the protection of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"19019","Mundhir ibn Amr al-Ansari, then al-Sa'idi, martyred on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah, commander of the detachment. 840 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr who said: Then the expedition of al-Mundhir ibn Amr, brother of Banu Sa'idah, to Bi'r Ma'unah, and he sent with them al-Muttalib al-Sulami to guide them on the way; the enemies of Allah sent to Amir ibn al-Tufayl seeking reinforcements and he reinforced them against the Muslims, so al-Mundhir ibn Amr and his companions were killed, except Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri whom they captured and spared until they brought him to Makkah, and he is the one who buried Khubayb ibn Adi; and the polytheists offered Urwah ibn al-Salt on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah to grant him safety and he refused, so they killed him. It was mentioned to us that the Muslims said on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah when the enemy surrounded them: O Allah, we find no one to convey from us to Thy Messenger but Thee, O Allah convey our greeting to him and inform him of our news."
"19020","841 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained after Uhud the rest of Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, Dhu al-Hijjah - the polytheists conducted that Hajj - and Muharram, then he sent the companions of Bi'r Ma'unah in Safar, four months after Uhud. Their account was as my father Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to me, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, and Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm and others among the people of knowledge, they said: Abu Bara Amir ibn Malik ibn Ja'far, Mula'ib al-Asinnah, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah and he presented Islam to him; he did not accept Islam nor was he far from Islam, and he said: O Muhammad, if you sent men of your companions to the people of Najd and they called them to faith, I hope they would respond to you, so send them to call the people to your cause. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent al-Mundhir ibn Amr, brother of Banu Sa'idah ibn Ka'b ibn al-Khazraj, who hastened to death, with forty men of the Muslims among their best, among them al-Harith ibn al-Simmah, Haram ibn Milhan brother of Banu Adi ibn al-Najjar, Urwah ibn Asma ibn al-Salt al-Sulami, Nafi' ibn Budayl ibn Warqa al-Khuza'i, Amir ibn Fuhayrah freedman of Abu Bakr, and named men among the best of the Muslims. They marched until they camped at Bi'r Ma'unah - between the land of Banu Amir and the lava field of Banu Sulaym, both lands close to it, and it is closer to Sulaym - and when they camped they sent Haram ibn Milhan with the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Amir ibn al-Tufayl; when he came to them he did not look at his letter before he attacked the man and killed him, then he called out Banu Amir against them but they refused to answer what he called them to, saying: We will not betray Abu Bara, for he made them a covenant and protection; so he called out against them the tribes of Banu Sulaym: Usayyah, Ri'l and Dhakwan, and they answered him, and they went out until they overwhelmed the people, surrounding them in their camp; when they saw them they took their swords and fought them until they were killed to the last of them, except Ka'b ibn Zayd brother of Banu Dinar ibn al-Najjar, whom they left with a breath of life, carried wounded from among the slain, and he lived until he was killed on the day of the Trench. In the grazing livestock of the people were Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri and a man of the Ansar, one of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and nothing informed them of the calamity of their brothers but birds hovering over the camp, and he said: By Allah, these birds are up to something; so they came to look and there were the people in their blood, and the horses that had struck them standing; the Ansari said to Amr ibn Umayyah: What do you think? He said: I think we join the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him of the news; the Ansari said: But I would not spare myself a place where al-Mundhir ibn Amr was killed, and men shall not tell me about him. Then he fought the people until he was killed, and Amr ibn Umayyah was taken captive; when he informed them he was from Mudar, Amir ibn al-Tufayl released him, cut his forelock, and freed him for a slave he claimed was due from his mother. Amr ibn Umayyah went out until at al-Qarqarah at the head of Qanah two men of Banu Amir came and camped with him in a shade he was in; the two Amiris had a covenant with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and protection, which Amr ibn Umayyah did not know; he asked them when they camped: From whom are you? They said: From Banu Amir; so he gave them respite until they slept, then attacked and killed them, thinking he had taken revenge by them on Banu Amir for what they had done to the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When Amr ibn Umayyah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you killed two protected men I will pay their blood money. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the deed of Abu Bara; I disliked it and feared it. That reached Abu Bara and Amir's betrayal of him grieved him, and what befell the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through his cause and protection. Hassan ibn Thabit said inciting Banu Abi Bara against Amir ibn al-Tufayl verses, and Rabi'ah ibn Amir charged Amir ibn al-Tufayl and stabbed him with the spear in the thigh, hamstrung him and he fell from his horse, and he said: This is the deed of Abu Bara; if I die my blood is for my uncle, let it not be pursued, and if I live I shall decide what to do about what was done to me."
"19021","Those named Marwan. Marwan ibn al-Hakam ibn al-As ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf. 842 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan ibn al-Hakam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions set out from al-Hudaybiyah with somewhat more than a hundred and ten of his companions, until when they were at Dhu al-Hulayfah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) garlanded the sacrificial animals and marked them, then entered ihram for umrah."
"19022","Marwan ibn Qays al-Asadi. 843 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Imran ibn Yahya al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: I heard my uncle Marwan ibn Qays - who had taken the governorship from his family in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - say: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father died, having vowed to walk to Makkah and to slaughter a camel, and he left no wealth; will it suffice for him if we walk on his behalf and fulfill a camel from my wealth? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, fulfill on his behalf, walk and slaughter; have you seen, if your father owed a debt to a man and you paid it from your wealth, would the man not go back satisfied? And Allah is more deserving to be pleased."
"19023","Those named Marzuq. Marzuq al-Sayqal. 844 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, Abu al-Hakam al-Sayqal narrated to me, Marzuq al-Sayqal narrated to me, that he polished the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Dhu al-Fiqar, which had a pommel of silver, rings in its scabbard and a ferrule in its middle of silver."
"19024","Those named Munkadir. Munkadir Abu Muhammad al-Taymi, Taym Quraysh. 845 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Hurayth ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever circumambulates the House seven times without idle talk, it is like freeing a slave."
"19025","846 - Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihraqani narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Murrah al-Jamali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he went out one night having delayed the Isha prayer until part of the night had gone, and the people were waiting in the mosque, and he said: What are you waiting for? They said: We are waiting for the prayer. He said: You are in prayer as long as you wait for it. Then he said: It is a prayer none of the nations before you prayed. Then he raised his head to the sky and said: The stars are security for the sky; if the stars are effaced there will come to the sky what it is promised, and I am security for my companions; when I am taken there will come to my companions what they are promised, and my companions are security for my ummah; when my companions are taken there will come to my ummah what it is promised. O Bilal, establish the prayer."
"19026","Those named Math'ab. Math'ab, without lineage. 847 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ya'ish narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from Math'ab who said: There was an expedition with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and none of them was without his mount which he took turns on except me; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would dismount then say to me: Ride, and I would say: I have strength, until he did that two or three times, then he said: You are but Math'ab. He said: So it became among the most beloved of my names to me. He said: I used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions, some of them fasting and some breaking fast, and neither did the fasting criticize the breaking nor the breaking the fasting."
"19027","Those named Mus'ab. Mus'ab ibn Umayr al-Qurashi then al-Adawi, Mus'ab ibn Umayr ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf ibn Abd al-Dar ibn Qusayy, among the first emigrants, martyred on the day of Uhud, from his reports. 848 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara who said: The first of the emigrants to come to us was Mus'ab ibn Umayr, one of Banu Abd al-Dar ibn Qusayy, and I said to him: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do? He said: He is in his place, and his companions are behind me."
"19028","849 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah who said: When the season came, a party of the Ansar performed Hajj, of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar among them: Mu'adh ibn Afra and As'ad ibn Zurarah; of Banu Zurayq: Rafi' ibn Malik and Dhakwan ibn Abd Qays; of Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan; of Banu Amr ibn Awf: Uwaym ibn Sa'idah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them and informed them of the news with which Allah had distinguished him of his prophethood and honor, and recited the Qur'an to them; when they heard his words they listened attentively, their souls were reassured to his call, and they recognized what they used to hear from the People of the Book of his mention in his description and what he called them to, so they believed him and believed in him, and they were among the causes of good. Then they said to him: You know of the blood between al-Aws and al-Khazraj, and we love the guidance by which Allah directs your affair, and we strive for Allah and for you; we counsel you with what you see, so stay in the name of Allah until we return to our people and inform them of your matter and call them to Allah and His Messenger; perhaps Allah will reconcile between us and unite our affair, for today we are distant and hateful to one another; if you come to us today while we are unreconciled we will have no unity upon you, but we promise you the season of next year. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted what they said, so they returned to their people and called them secretly and informed them of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what Allah sent him with, calling to it with the Qur'an, until hardly a house of the Ansar remained but people in it had become Muslim. Then they sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Send to us a man from you to call the people with the Book of Allah, for it is more likely to be followed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to them Mus'ab ibn Umayr brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, and he stayed in Banu Ghanm with As'ad ibn Zurarah, calling the people secretly, Islam spreading and its people increasing, while concealing their call. Then As'ad ibn Zurarah came with Mus'ab ibn Umayr until they reached Bi'r Murri - or near it - and they sat there and sent to a group of the people of the land who came to them secretly; while Mus'ab ibn Umayr was narrating to them and reciting the Qur'an to them, Sa'd ibn Mu'adh was informed of them, and he came to them in his armor with a spear until he stood over them and said: Why does this solitary, isolated, outcast stranger come to our homes to mislead our weak with falsehood and call them to it? I shall not see you after this with any of our protection. So they left, then they returned a second time at Bi'r Murri - or near it - and Sa'd ibn Mu'adh was informed of them a second time and threatened them with less than the first threat; when As'ad saw leniency from him he said: O son of my maternal aunt, hear his words; if you hear evil, reject it, and if you hear good, accept it. He said: What does he say? So Mus'ab ibn Umayr recited to them: Ha Mim, by the clear Book, We made it an Arabic Qur'an that you may understand. Sa'd ibn Mu'adh said: I hear nothing but what I recognize. He returned, Allah having guided him, without showing them Islam until he returned to his people; he called Banu Abd al-Ashhal to Islam, showed his Islam, and said: Whoever of young or old, male or female doubts it, let him bring us better guidance than it and we shall take it; by Allah, a matter has come in which necks will grieve. So Banu Abd al-Ashhal became Muslim at Sa'd's Islam and call - except those not mentioned - and it was the first of the houses of the Ansar to become Muslim in its entirety. Then Banu al-Najjar expelled Mus'ab ibn Umayr and were harsh with As'ad ibn Zurarah, so Mus'ab ibn Umayr moved to Sa'd ibn Mu'adh and remained with him calling, Allah guiding at his hands, until hardly a house of the Ansar remained but people in it had become Muslim, their nobles became Muslim, Amr ibn al-Jamuh became Muslim, their idols were broken, the Muslims were the mightiest of its people, their affair was set right, and Mus'ab ibn Umayr returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he was called al-Muqri."
"19029","850 - Amr ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from Futn ibn Wahb, from Abd Allah ibn Umayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Mus'ab ibn Umayr when he returned from Uhud, stood over him and his companions and said: I bear witness that you are alive with Allah, so return them and pray over them; by Him in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, none greets them but they return it to him until the Day of Resurrection."
"19030","Mus'ab al-Aslami. 851 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrate, from Mus'ab al-Aslami who said: A youth of ours went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I ask you a question. He said: What is it? He said: I ask you to make me among those for whom you intercede on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Who ordered you with this - or who taught you this? - or who guided you to this? He said: No one ordered me with this but myself. He said: You are among those for whom I intercede on the Day of Resurrection. The youth went off joyful to inform his family; when he turned he said: Bring the youth back to me. They brought him back gloomy, fearing something had occurred about him. He said: Help me for yourself with much prostration."
"19031","Those named Ma'dan. Ma'dan Abu Khalid, said to have companionship. 852 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Rihabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ziyad, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Gentle, loves gentleness, approves it and aids upon it what He does not aid upon harshness. When you ride these non-speaking mounts, give them their rests; if the land is barren then move on upon them, for the land is folded at night what is not folded by day. Beware of stopping to rest on the road, for it is the path of mounts and shelter of snakes."
"19032","Those named Makhlad. Makhlad al-Ghifari. 853 - Ahmad ibn al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, from Makhlad al-Ghifari, that three slaves of Banu Ghifar witnessed Badr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umar used to give them a thousand to each man."
"19033","Those named al-Mughirah. Mughirah Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf, accepted Islam on the day of the Conquest, met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the way and was among those who stood firm with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn. Died in year twenty. 854 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Kathir ibn al-Abbas, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith on the day of Hunayn and said: Who are you? He said: Son of thy mother. And he spoke good to him."
"19034","Mughirah ibn Shu'bah al-Thaqafi. 855 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah ibn Abi Amir ibn Mas'ud ibn Mu'attib ibn Malik ibn Ka'b ibn Amr ibn Ma'd ibn Awf ibn Qays ibn Munabbih, kunyah Abu Abd Allah, his mother a woman of Banu Nasr ibn Mu'awiyah; he governed Basrah about two years, then governed Kufah and died there in year fifty. His first battle with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was al-Hudaybiyah."
"19035","856 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Al-Mughirah died in year fifty."
"19036","857 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab first sent to Kufah Abu Ubayd al-Thaqafi - father of al-Mukhtar - and he was killed; then he sent Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas and he stayed five years then removed him; then he sent Ammar ibn Yasir and he stayed a year then removed him; and he sent al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah and he stayed a year, then Umar was killed. When Uthman took charge he sent Sa'd to Kufah and he stayed a year then removed him; and he sent al-Walid ibn Uqbah and he stayed five years then removed him; and he sent Sa'id ibn al-As and he stayed five years then removed him; and he sent Abu Musa al-Ash'ari and he stayed a year, then Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed and there was tribulation. Then the first whom Mu'awiyah appointed over Kufah was al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah for nine years then he died; then he sent Ziyad ibn Abih and he stayed four years then died; then he sent al-Dahhak ibn Qays and he stayed three years then removed him; then he sent al-Nu'man ibn Bashir and he stayed four months then Mu'awiyah died and there was tribulation. Then came the affair of Muslim ibn Aqil and his companions."
"19037","What al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah transmitted. Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 858 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for his need, and I went with him with a water skin; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a Syrian cloak. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his need, he performed ablution and wiped over the two leather socks."
"19038","859 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mu'an ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said about the hide of carrion: Its tanning is its purification."
"19039","Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from al-Mughirah. 860 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that Umar consulted the people about the miscarriage of a woman, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge with a ghurrah: a slave or a slave-girl. He said: Do you bring one to testify with you? So Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified for him."
"19040","Qurrah ibn Iyas al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah. 861 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge, Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi, and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, they said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Abu Iyas Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to me, from his father Qurrah who said: In the days of al-Qadisiyah, al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah sent to the master of Persia saying: Send ten with me. He said: So he tightened his clothes and took a shield with him, then went until they came to him; he said to the people: Throw me a cloak and he sat upon it. The foreigner said: You Arabs, I know what brought you here; you are a people who do not find in your land food to satisfy yourselves, so take, we shall give you food you need; we are Magians and we dislike killing you, you covet our land. Al-Mughirah said: By Allah, that is not what brought us, but we were a people worshipping stones and idols; when we saw a stone better than a stone we cast it and took another, and we knew no Lord until Allah sent to us a messenger from ourselves who called us to Islam and we followed him, and he ordered us to fight our enemy among those who abandoned Islam. We did not come for food but we came to kill your fighters and take your offspring captive. As for what you mentioned of food, by my life we did not find food to satisfy us, and sometimes we did not find water to quench thirst; we came to this land of yours and found much food in it; by Allah we shall not leave it until it is ours or yours. The foreigner said in Persian: He spoke truth, and thine eye will be gouged tomorrow at al-Qadisiyah. His eye was gouged the next day, struck by an arrow."
"19041","Abu Firas al-Aslami, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 862 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Salt ibn Muhammad al-Kharaki narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Farwah narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abu Firas, a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking women, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go to so-and-so and look at what they have, for it is more lasting for love; if you are pleased with her I shall marry you. So I came to them and greeted them, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, ordering you to show her to me? I said: Yes. So she uncovered her curtain, and said: Look. So I married her, and I never married anything more beloved to me than her, though I married sixty women."
"19042","Ibn Abi Marhab, having companionship, from al-Mughirah. 863 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of the Maghazi, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Sa'id al-Thawri narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abi Marhab who said: Four descended into the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf; and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah used to be called the most recent of people in covenant with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so that I be the last of people in covenant with him."
"19043","Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father. Al-Sha'bi, from Urwah. 864 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Amir, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night on a journey and he said: Hast thou water? I said: Yes. He dismounted his mount and walked until hidden from me in the darkness of night, then came, and I poured upon him from the water of the skin; he washed his hands and face, wearing a woolen cloak, and could not bring his arms out of its narrowness until he brought them out from under the cloak; he washed his arms and wiped his head. Then I stooped to remove his leather socks, and he said: Leave them, for I put them on pure. And he wiped over them."
"19044","865 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he performed ablution and wiped over his two leather socks."
"19045","866 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he dismounted and said: Is there purification water? I brought him water and he washed his hands and face, then went to wash his arms but the cloak constrained him, a cloak of the cloaks of Rome; he drew his hands from under the cloak, washed his arms, and I stooped to the leather socks, and he said: Leave the leather socks, for I put the feet into the leather socks while pure. And he wiped over the leather socks."
"19046","867 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn and Yunus, from Abu Ishaq, and Zakariyya ibn Abi Yahya, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, dost thou wipe over thy leather socks? He said: Yes, I put them on while pure."
"19047","868 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father who said: We were on a journey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Hast thou water? I said: Yes. He dismounted his mount then walked until hidden from me; when he came I met him with the purification vessel, and he performed ablution, washed his hands and face, wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves; he brought his hand out from under the cloak, washed his arms and wiped his head. Then I stooped to his leather socks to remove them, and he said: Leave them, for I put them on while pure. And he wiped over his leather socks."
"19048","869 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father who said: I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night and he said: Who is this? I said: I am al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. He said: Hold. So I held his she-camel for him and he went on until I saw him not; then he came and I performed his ablution, uncovering his arms; the sleeve of the cloak was narrow, so he brought his hands out from under it, performed ablution, washed his hands, face and arms, and wiped over his leather socks. I said: Wilt thou not remove thy leather socks? He said: I put them on pure."
"19049","870 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad and al-Sha'bi - Ibn Awn said: I do not retain the hadith of this from the hadith of that, and the hadith of al-Sha'bi was the closer in chain - al-Sha'bi narrated, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, and Muhammad referred the hadith to al-Mughirah - Ibn Awn said: He mentioned that journey - he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tapped my back with a stick with him, and he turned aside and I turned aside until we reached - I know not where on earth - and he made the camel kneel and dismounted and went on until hidden from me. Then he came and said: Hast thou water? And I had a small vessel; I poured upon him and he washed his hands and face, and went to wash his arms wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves; he brought his hands out from under the body, washed his hands and face, washed his arms and wiped - Ibn Awn said: And he mentioned something of his forelock and turban, I know not whether I got it right - and wiped over his leather socks, then said: Thy need? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no need. We went on and came to the people, and Ibn Awf had led them in the dawn prayer, praying a rak'ah with them; I went to inform him and he stopped me. So we prayed what we caught and made up what we missed."
"19050","871 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid and Mujalid, from Amir al-Sha'bi, Urwah ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me, from his father who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he stood for his need wearing a Roman cloak, performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, and said: I wore them while in purity."
"19051","872 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Baghdadi, and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Asbat al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hammad narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Amir, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: I performed the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he wiped over his leather socks, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, hast thou forgotten? He said: Rather thou hast forgotten; with this my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me."
"19052","873 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Rihabi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hakim al-Muqawwim narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated to us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he heard his father say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he went for his need, then gestured to me and I brought him water, wearing a Syrian cloak without sleeves; he cast it over his shoulder and said: Pour upon me. So I poured upon him and he performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks. And it was a sunnah: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"19053","874 - Muhammad ibn Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Sulaym, freedman of al-Sha'bi, narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19054","Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 875 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Layth informed us; (ha) and al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he went out for his need and al-Mughirah followed him with the water skin containing water; he poured upon him until he finished his need, then performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."
"19055","876 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to him, that Nafi' ibn Jubayr narrated to him, that Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to him, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."
"19056","877 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."
"19057","878 - Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah, that he poured upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his vessel; he washed his face, then went to wash his arms but the sleeves were narrow for his arms, so he brought them out from under the cloak, which was of wool, then washed them and wiped over his leather socks."
"19058","879 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"19059","Abbad ibn Ziyad, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah. 880 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Abbad ibn Ziyad, that Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah informed him that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah informed him, that he raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the raid of Tabuk; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieved himself before the privy place, and I carried with him a water skin before the dawn prayer. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to me I poured upon his hands from the skin; he washed his hands three times, then rinsed and sniffed, then washed his face, then went to bring his cloak out from his arms but the sleeves of his cloak were narrow, so he put his hands into the cloak to the elbows, then performed ablution over his leather socks. Then he came forward and I came forward with him until we found the people had put Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf forward leading them; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught one of the two rak'ahs and prayed with the people the last rak'ah. When Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf greeted, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to complete his prayer, which startled the Muslims and they glorified much. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he turned to them and said: Ye did well - or he said: Ye did right - envying them for praying the prayer in its time. Ibn Shihab said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, the like of the hadith of Abbad ibn Ziyad. And he added: Al-Mughirah said: I hastened to inform Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him. And he mentioned the like of it."
"19060","881 - Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abbad ibn Ziyad, from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."
"19061","Abu al-Zinad, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah. 882 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dulabi narrated to us; (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn the judge narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over the upper part of the leather socks."
"19062","883 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Husayn the judge narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, consulted them about the miscarriage of a woman - meaning the fallen fetus - al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: So I said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged therein with a ghurrah. Umar said: If thou art truthful bring one who knows that. So I brought Muhammad ibn Maslamah and he came and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged therein with a ghurrah."
"19063","Umar ibn Bayan al-Taghlibi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah. 884 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi narrated to us, Tu'mah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Umar ibn Bayan al-Taghlibi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells wine, let him cut up the pigs."
"19064","Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father. 885 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over the turban and the two leather socks."
"19065","886 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us; (ha) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah, from al-Hasan, from Ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his forelock."
"19066","887 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Bakr, from Ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks, wiped the front of his head, placed his hands upon the turban, and wiped over the turban; and he did not mention al-Hasan."
"19067","888 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Bakr, from Ibn al-Mughirah, from his father, the like of it; and he did not mention al-Hasan."
"19068","889 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to me, from his father who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and he said: Stay back O Mughirah, and go on O people. He said: Then he went and relieved his need and I brought him a water skin; when he finished I poured upon him from it and he washed his face, then went to bring his hands out of a Roman cloak upon him, but the sleeves of the cloak were narrow, so he brought his hands out from under the cloak and washed them, then wiped over his leather socks, then prayed."
"19069","Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah, from his father. 890 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Husayn the judge narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father as a narration, who said: He did not rely who seeks ruqyah or cauterization."
"19070","891 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us; (ha) and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barrah al-San'ani narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He did not rely who is cauterized or seeks ruqyah."
"19071","892 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Hassan ibn Abi Wahrah, Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, from his father al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He did not rely who seeks ruqyah or cauterization."
"19072","893 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Zayd ibn Harithah, from Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged for the fetus a ghurrah: a slave or a slave-girl."
"19073","Al-Mughirah son of al-Mughirah's daughter, from al-Mughirah. 894 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Nawfal narrated to us, from al-Mughirah son of al-Mughirah's daughter who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah passed by al-Hirah and there were people who had set up a fox shooting at it as a target; he stood over them and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid mutilation."
"19074","Al-Aswad ibn Abi Asim al-Thaqafi, from al-Mughirah. 895 - Abu Ghassan Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn al-Walid al-Ahwazi narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Nawfal ibn Umarah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Aswad ibn Abi Asim al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn stand over a slain man of Thaqif and say: May Allah remove thee far, for thou used to hate Quraysh."
"19075","Warrad freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. Al-Sha'bi, from Warrad freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah. 896 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Talib narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Shibak, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he finished his prayer would say: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19076","897 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Rashid al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, Zakariyya, Isma'il and Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad who said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan wrote to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: Write to me something thou heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So al-Mughirah wrote to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at the end of prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee. And he used to forbid idle talk, much questioning, wasting wealth, withholding and demanding, disobedience to mothers, and burying daughters alive."
"19077","898 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Dawud and Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad scribe of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah who said: Mu'awiyah wrote to him: Write to me something thou heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the end of prayer. So he said: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19078","899 - Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he finished prayer would say: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19079","900 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me; (ha) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, Ibn al-Ashwa' narrated to me, from al-Sha'bi, the scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah: Write to me something thou heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to him: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah disliked for you three: idle talk, much questioning, and wasting wealth."
"19080","901 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Imran narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forbade you disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding; and He disliked for you idle talk, much questioning, and wasting wealth."
"19081","902 - Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us; (ha) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah the Exalted disliked idle talk, much questioning, and wasting wealth; and forbade burying daughters alive, disobedience to mothers, and withholding and demanding."
"19082","903 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us; (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah disliked for you three: idle talk, much questioning, and wasting wealth; and forbade disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding."
"19083","904 - Abu Husayn the judge narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19084","905 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Musa ibn Sufyan al-Junday Saburi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a group of the Ansar shooting a pigeon and said: Do not take a living soul as a target."
"19085","Al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Warrad. 906 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Warrad, from al-Mughirah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he finished prayer would say: There is no god but Allah... and he mentioned the hadith."
"19086","907 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Warrad scribe of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, like the hadith of Mansur."
"19087","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad. 908 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, Warrad, scribe of al-Mughirah, informed me, he said: Al-Mughirah wrote to Mu'awiyah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful."
"19088","909 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, who said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan wrote to al-Mughirah: Write to me something of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seek refuge from three: from disobedience to mothers, from burying daughters alive, and from withholding and demanding; and I heard him forbid three: idle talk, wasting wealth, and much questioning; and I heard him say: O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19089","910 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of the hadith of Ma'mar."
"19090","911 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah, that he wrote to Mu'awiyah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he greeted would say: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19091","912 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad who said: Al-Mughirah wrote to Mu'awiyah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19092","913 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, scribe of al-Mughirah, that Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah: Write to me something thou heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade idle talk, much questioning, and wasting wealth; and forbade disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding."
"19093","914 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, with Ibn Abi Lubabah present, they heard Warrad, scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, say: Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah: Write to me something thou heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say after prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after his prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19094","915 - Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Sinan al-Rahawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say after prayer, and he mentioned the like of it."
"19095","916 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19096","917 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19097","918 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after prayer when he greeted: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19098","919 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Bashir narrated to us, Amr ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad who said: Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah: Write to me something thou heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to him in my handwriting: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he finished prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee. And he wrote to him in the letter: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted disliked for you three: burying daughters alive, disobedience to mothers, and withholding and demanding; and he used to forbid idle talk, much questioning, and wasting wealth."
"19099","920 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan al-Kufi narrated to us, Malik ibn Su'ayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr and al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Warrad, from al-Mughirah, the like of it."
"19100","921 - Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: Sa'd ibn Ubadah said: If I saw a man with my wife I would strike him with the sword. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do you wonder at the jealousy of Sa'd? By Allah, I am more jealous than Sa'd, and Allah is more jealous than me. For that reason He forbade indecencies, what is apparent and what is hidden thereof. And no person loves excuse more than Allah, Mighty and Majestic; for that reason He sent His messengers as bearers of glad tidings and warners. And no person loves praise more than Allah, Mighty and Majestic; for that He promised Paradise. And the wording is of the hadith of Abu al-Walid."
"19101","922 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: It reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Sa'd ibn Ubadah says: If I found a man with her I would strike him with the sword unsparingly. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you wonder at the jealousy of Sa'd? By Allah... and he mentioned the like of the hadith."
"19102","923 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us; (ha) and Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, they said: al-Hakam ibn Hisham al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to me, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he struck his hand upon the neck of my mount, then said: Hast thou water? I said: Yes, this flat vessel of water with me. He said: Leave it. Then he dismounted, relieved the need, then came to me and said: Dost thou need? I said: No. He said: So he washed his hands thrice, rinsed thrice, sniffed thrice, then washed his face thrice, then wanted to bring his arms out, wearing a narrow woolen cloak, unable to bring his arms out of it; so he brought his hands out from under the cloak, then washed his arms thrice thrice, then wiped his head and wiped over the leather socks. Then we traveled and caught up with the people with Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf leading them; I wanted to inform him of the place of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he stopped me. So we prayed with him a rak'ah, then made up the second. And the wording is of the hadith of Hisham ibn Ammar."
"19103","Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Warrad freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah. 924 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah informed me, that Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, informed him, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wrote to Mu'awiyah - Warrad wrote that letter for him -: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say when he greets: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19104","Al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Warrad. 925 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Husayn the judge narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us; (ha) and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from the freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he wrote to Mu'awiyah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he greeted from prayer would say: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19105","926 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is Living, undying, in His hand is good, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19106","927 - Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Wahb al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn al-Harith al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Warrad who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wrote to Mu'awiyah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he finished prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19107","928 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar al-Basri narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Musayyib, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19108","Sulaym ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Warrad. 929 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Musayyib narrated to us, from Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nakha'i, from Warrad, scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah asking him about the last words the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say. So he wrote to him that he used to say when he greeted: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee, after greeting to his right and to his left; and he used to greet to his right until the whiteness of his right cheek was seen, and to his left until the whiteness of his left cheek was seen."
"19109","Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Warrad. 930 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha al-Asbahani narrated to us, Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of idle talk, withholding and demanding, disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and wasting wealth."
"19110","Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Warrad. 931 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir narrated to me, that Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, narrated to me, he said: Al-Mughirah ordered me to write to Mu'awiyah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after every prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19111","Makhul al-Shami, from Warrad. 932 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, Yazid ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, that Makhul narrated to them, from the freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah - I thought he named him Warrad - from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this hadith."
"19112","933 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Mukassir narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Makhul, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah asking him what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he finished prayer. So al-Mughirah wrote to him that he used to say when he greeted: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19113","Abu Sa'id, from Warrad. 934 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id who said: Warrad, scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, informed me, that Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: Write to me something thou heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to him: When he prayed and finished he would say: There is no god but Allah alone without partner - Ibn Awn said: I think he said: - to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19114","935 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri and Ibn Awn, from al-Warrad, from al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it; and he did not mention Abu Sa'id."
"19115","Abd Rabbihi, from Warrad. 936 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abd Rabbihi, from the scribe of al-Mughirah, that al-Mughirah wrote to Mu'awiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after his prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19116","Raja ibn Haywah, from Warrad. 937 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Raja ibn Haywah, from the scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan wrote to al-Mughirah asking him: Hast thou heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he says after prayer? So al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say after prayer: There is no god but Allah alone without partner. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19117","938 - Sulayman ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Qasim ibn Ma'n narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Raja ibn Haywah, from the scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything after prayer? He said: He used to say: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what Thou givest, none gives what Thou withholdest, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against Thee."
"19118","939 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us; and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Raja ibn Haywah, from the scribe of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the top of the leather sock and its bottom."
"19119","Narration of the Kufans, from al-Mughirah. Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi, from Warrad. 940 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi both narrated to us, they said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, from Warrad, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: A woman was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had struck her co-wife with a pole and killed her, and killed what was in her womb. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed her blood money upon the woman's male relatives, and for the fetus a ghurrah: a slave or a slave-girl. A man of the people stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we pay blood money for one who neither ate nor drank, nor cried nor wailed? He said: This one speaks with the speech of a soothsayer; therein is a ghurrah: a slave or a slave-girl."
"19120","941 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it; and he did not mention Warrad."
"19121","942 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us; (ha) and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, all of them from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade three: disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding; and forbade idle talk: much questioning, and wasting wealth."
"19122","943 - Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, al-Furat ibn Khalid narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi narrate, from Warrad, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that Mu'awiyah wrote to him asking him what he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, disliked for you three: disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding; and idle talk, much questioning, and wasting wealth."
"19123","Masruq ibn al-Ajda', from al-Mughirah. 944 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; (ha) and Abu Husayn the judge narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim, from Masruq, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and he said: O Mughirah, take the water skin. So I took it then went out with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on until hidden from me and relieved his need. Then he came wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves; he went to bring his hand out of its sleeve but it was narrow, and he brought his hand out from under it. So I poured upon him, and he performed ablution for prayer and wiped over his leather socks, then prayed."
"19124","945 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that he performed the ablution of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks and over the head cover."
"19125","946 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ziyad al-Ubulli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Hurayth, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and relieved himself; I followed him with a water skin with me. When he finished I poured upon him; he washed his face, wearing a Roman - or Syrian - cloak; its sleeve was narrow, so he brought his hand out from under it, washed his arms, and wiped over the turban and the leather socks."
"19126","Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah. Al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, from Qays. 947 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Mughirah ibn Shibl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam forgets and stands fully upright, upon him are the two prostrations of forgetfulness; and when he does not stand fully upright, there is no forgetfulness prostration upon him."
"19127","Bayan ibn Bishr, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim. 948 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: None asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: What wilt thou do? He will not harm thee. I said: Shall I not kill Ibn Sayyad? He said: What wilt thou do by killing him? If he is the Dajjal thou shalt not get to kill him, and if he is not the Dajjal what wilt thou do with him?"
"19128","949 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Bayan, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: We used to pray with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the noon prayer in the midday heat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Cool the prayer, for intense heat is from the blast of Hell."
"19129","Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim. 950 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: None asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Dajjal more than I asked him. So the Prophet of Allah said: What is thy question about him? He will not harm thee."
"19130","951 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: None asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than I asked him about him - meaning the Dajjal - and he said: He will not harm thee. I said: They say with him is a river and such. He said: He is more insignificant to Allah than that."
"19131","952 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Shihab ibn Abbad al-Abdi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: None asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Dajjal more than I asked him; and he mentioned the like of it."
"19132","953 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: None asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: What is thy question about him? Thou shalt not live to see him; he shall not emerge until no inheritance is divided and no spoils are taken joyfully."
"19133","954 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Qays narrated to me, al-Mughirah narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not asked about the Dajjal more than I asked him. And he said to me: What harmeth thee from him? I said: They say with him is a mountain of bread and a river of water. He said: He is more insignificant to Allah than that."
"19134","955 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, it reached me that with the Dajjal are rivers of water and mountains of bread. He said: He is more insignificant to Allah than that. So I was among the most questioning of people about him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: He is not what harmeth thee."
"19135","956 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us; (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, both from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not asked about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: O my son, what shall befall thee from him? I said: The people say with him is food and drink. He said: He is more insignificant to Allah than that."
"19136","957 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Mughirah who said: None asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: Why dost thou ask me about him? He said: I said: The people say with him is Paradise and Fire, and food and drink. He said: He is more insignificant to Allah than that."
"19137","958 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah who said: None asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: What troubleth thee from him that thou askest about him? He will not harm thee. So I said: They claim with him are rivers and food. He said: He is more insignificant to Allah than that."
"19138","959 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall not cease people of my ummah dominant over the people, until Allah's command comes to them while dominant."
"19139","960 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Waki', Abu Usamah and Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us; (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, all of them from Isma'il, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall not cease among my ummah a people dominant until Allah's command comes to them while dominant."
"19140","961 - Abu Husayn the judge narrated to us, al-Himmani narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall not cease a party of my ummah upon the truth, dominant, until the Hour comes."
"19141","962 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Some people of my ummah will remain dominant until the command of Allah comes to them while they are dominant."""
"19142","963 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah informed me, he said: I was with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) when a horse was presented to him, and a man said: Mount me on this. He said: For me to mount a boy who has already ridden horses bareback is dearer to me than mounting you on it. The man became angry and said: By Allah, I am better than you and your father as a horseman. I became angry when he said that to the caliph of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I rose to him, seized him by the head and dragged him on his nose, until his nose was as if it were the spout of a waterskin. The Ansar wanted to exact retaliation from me for it, and that reached Abu Bakr, and he said: It has reached me that some people claim I will let them retaliate against al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah; for me to expel them from their homes is nearer than letting them retaliate against one of the restrainers of Allah by whom He restrains His servants."""
"19143","964 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from al-Mughirah: that he was standing at the head of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a sword while he was veiled, and Urwah kept reaching for the beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was speaking, so al-Mughirah said to him: You will surely withhold your hand or it will not return to you - and al-Mughirah was wearing a sword - so Urwah said: O Messenger of Allah, who is this? He said: ""This is the son of your brother, al-Mughirah."" He said: O treacherous one, I have not yet washed my head from your treachery."
"19144","965 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A single suckling does not make unlawful."" We said: What is the single suckling? He said: ""A woman gives birth and milk gathers in her breast, and she nurses her neighbor woman's child once or twice."""
"19145","Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salamah from al-Mughirah. 966 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, (H) and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah and Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Mughirah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the rubbish heap of so-and-so tribe, spread his legs and urinated standing."
"19146","967 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, (H) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Ali ibn Ma'bad narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the rubbish heap of a people, so I brought him water and he performed ablution while wearing a small-sleeved Roman cloak; he brought his hand out from under that cloak, washed his face, wiped his head and wiped over his leather socks, then stood and prayed."
"19147","968 - al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated at the rubbish heap of so-and-so tribe and said: ""O Mughirah, do you have water with you?"" He said: Yes, a waterskin of water. And he was wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves, so he performed ablution and wiped over his feet while wearing leather socks."
"19148","969 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Shu'bah: Asim ibn Bahdalah informed me, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the rubbish heap of a people and urinated standing."
"19149","970 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hammad ibn Numayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, he said: I witnessed al-Qadisiyyah, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah went forth, and when he drew near the throne of Rustum he leapt and sat with him on his throne, and they grunted in disapproval. Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said to them: What frightens you of this? I shall now stand and return to what I was upon, and your companion will return to what he was upon. They said: Tell us what brought you. Al-Mughirah said: We were astray, then Allah sent among us a Prophet and guided us to His religion, and among what He provided us was a grain found in this land of yours; when we ate from it and fed our families, they said: We cannot bear patience until you settle us in this land. They said: Then we shall kill you. He said: If you kill us we enter Paradise, and if we kill you you enter the Fire."""
"19150","al-Aswad ibn Hilal from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 971 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (H) and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted and relieved himself, then came, and I poured water for him from a waterskin I had with me, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."""
"19151","Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd and Abu Sufyan Talhah ibn Nafi' from al-Mughirah. 972 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Shuja' ibn Makhlad narrated to us, (H) and Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, they said: Hushaym narrated to us: Husayn informed us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd and Abu Sufyan, that they heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrating, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he went aside to relieve himself; when he finished I came to him with a waterskin containing water, poured for him and he performed ablution. He was wearing a cloak with narrow sleeves, so he brought his hand out from under the cloak, washed his forearms and wiped over his leather socks."
"19152","973 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Sufyan, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah hears whoever praises Him,"" he would say: ""O Allah, none can withhold what You give, none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."""
"19153","Ali ibn Rabi'ah al-Walibi from al-Mughirah. 974 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, he said: The first over whom wailing was done in Kufah was Qarazah ibn Ka'b al-Ansari, and he claimed that al-Mughirah stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire,"" and I heard him say: ""Whoever is wailed over, he is punished for what is wailed over him."""
"19154","975 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ubayd al-Ta'i narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Lying upon me is not like lying upon anyone else."""
"19155","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"19156","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When wailing is done over the dead, he is punished on account of the wailing done over him."""
"19157","976 - Amr ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"19158","977 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Jarir narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"19159","Ubayd ibn Nudaylah al-Khuza'i from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 978 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah al-Khuza'i, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: A co-wife struck her co-wife with a tent pole and killed her, so it was judged that her blood-money be upon the killer's paternal relatives, and for what was in her womb a ghurrah (a slave or slave-girl). The bedouin said: Do you impose a fine on me for one who neither ate nor drank, nor cried out and uttered a sound? Is the like of that to go unrequited? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is it rhymed speech like the rhymed speech of the bedouins?"" Abu Hudhayfah added in his hadith: And it was judged for what was in her womb a ghurrah."
"19160","979 - Daran ibn Sufyan al-Qattan al-Basri narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: A man of Hudhayl had two wives, and one of them threw at the other a millstone or a tent pole and caused her to miscarry. That was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in it a ghurrah. Her guardians said: How can we pay blood-money for one who neither cried out nor uttered a sound, neither drank nor ate? Is the like of that to go unrequited? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is it rhymed speech like the rhymed speech of the bedouins?"" And he judged its blood-money upon the guardians of the woman."
"19161","980 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19162","981 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (H) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Ya'la Abu al-Muhayyah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19163","982 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19164","983 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Harb al-Saffar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Ubayd ibn Nudaylah, from al-Mughirah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19165","Bishr ibn Quhayf from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 984 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Bishr ibn Quhayf, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: While I was traveling one night, I heard the grunting of a rider among the riders. Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: I said: Who are you? He said: ""I am the Messenger of Allah."" So I held back until he caught up with me, and I rode alongside him. Then he dismounted and relieved himself. He said: ""Do you have water with you?"" I said: Would it harm you? He said: ""So I brought him water, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, and we did not part until we had prayed the dawn prayer."
"19166","985 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (H) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Quhayf, he said: We were in the house of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, and they mentioned purification, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieve himself, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."
"19167","Alqamah ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 986 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, (H) and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Imran ibn Maysarah al-Awdi narrated to us, (H) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Najran, and they said to me among what they said: In what you recite there is: ""O sister of Harun"" - and between Musa and Isa there was what you know? He said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: ""Why did you not inform them that they used to name themselves with their names and with the righteous who were before them?"""
"19168","Amir al-Sha'bi from al-Mughirah. 987 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that he stood up in the first two rak'ahs, and they glorified Allah to alert him but he did not sit; when he finished his prayer he prostrated twice after the salutation, then said: Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"19169","988 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronounced the tashahhud when he raised his head from the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"19170","989 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (H) and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif and Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Abjar, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah - Ibn Abjar raised it (to the Prophet) and Mutarrif did not raise it - he said: Musa (peace be upon him) said: O Lord, inform me of the lowest of the people of Paradise in rank. He said: Yes, he is a man who will come after the people have taken their dwellings and received their shares, and it will be said to him: Enter Paradise. He will say: O Lord, how can I enter it when the people have taken their dwellings and received their shares? He will say: Would you be pleased for you to have the like of what a king among the kings of this world had? He will say: I am pleased, my Lord. He will say: You shall have the like of it and the like of it and the like of it - and Sufyan clasped his five fingers - and he will say: I am pleased. He will say: You shall have this and whatever your soul desires and your eye delights in. He will say: I am pleased, my Lord. Musa said: O Lord, then inform me of the highest of the people of Paradise in rank. He said: Yes, those are the ones I intended, and I shall inform you of them: I planted their honor with My hand and sealed it, so no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and it has not occurred to the heart of a human."" And the confirmation of that in the Book of Allah is: ""No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort of eyes as reward for what they used to do."""
"19171","990 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Mughirah while he was addressing from the pulpit, saying: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign, and he went off for his need, so I followed him with a waterskin; he brought his hands out of a cloak he was wearing with narrow sleeves, bringing them out from beneath it, washed his face and hands, wiped his head and wiped over his leather socks."
"19172","991 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, (H) and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, (H) and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Abbas, from al-Shaybani, from Amir, he said: It was said to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: From where did the Prophet have leather socks? He said: ""Dihyah al-Kalbi gifted them to him."""
"19173","992 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from his father, he said: When al-Sha'bi narrated the hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks, I said: O Abu Amr, and from where did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have leather socks? He said: Dihyah al-Kalbi gifted them to him."
"19174","993 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah and Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri' narrated to us, all of them from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was among those who dug the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""So we made a lahd (niche grave) for him, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was entered into the grave, I threw down the pickaxe, then said: The pickaxe, the pickaxe - so I went down and placed my hand on the niche."" And al-Mughirah used to say: ""I am the last of the people to be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"19175","994 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, he said: A man said in the presence of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: May Allah bless Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets, there is no prophet after him. Al-Mughirah said: ""It suffices you to say: Seal of the Prophets, for we used to narrate that Isa son of Maryam will come forth; if he comes forth, then he was before him and after him."""
"19176","Huzayl ibn Shurahbil from al-Mughirah. 995 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks."
"19177","996 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, my father and Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak and Waki' and Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to me, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated, performed ablution and wiped over his socks and sandals."
"19178","Sa'd ibn Ubaydah from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. 997 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his campaigns, and he dismounted for his need, so I brought him water for ablution; he was wearing a tight cloak, brought his hand out from under it, I poured for him, he performed ablution and wiped his leather socks."
"19179","Thabit ibn Ubayd from al-Mughirah. 998 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani informed us, Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, he said: I prayed behind al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah and he did not sit in the second (rak'ah); the people glorified Allah to alert him and he continued in his prayer. When he finished his prayer he prostrated twice then gave the salutation, then turned to the people and said: Had you glorified Allah before I stood upright, I would have sat, but thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray with us."
"19180","Ubaydullah al-Thaqafi from al-Mughirah. 999 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Yunus ibn al-Harith al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah Abu Awn al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to pray on a tanned fur or a mat."
"19181","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm Abu al-Hakam al-Bajali from al-Mughirah. 1000 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Amir narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm, claiming that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrated to him that he walked with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came to one of those valleys, entered it and relieved himself, then came out, performed ablution and removed the leather socks; when he put them on he then perceived a smell, so he returned, performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks. I said: Did you forget, O Prophet of Allah? He said: ""No, rather you forgot; with this did my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, command me."""
"19182","1001 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Amir al-Bajali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you forget? He said: ""Rather you forgot; with this did my Lord command me."""
"19183","1002 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali and my father narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Amir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you forget? He said: ""Rather you forgot; with this did my Lord command me."""
"19184","Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa from al-Mughirah. 1003 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb and Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, they said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I ate one day then came to the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he said: ""Whoever eats anything of this tree, let him not approach our mosque."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, give me your hand - so I put it inside my chest (garment) and he saw it bandaged, and he said: ""Except for an excuse."""
"19185","1004 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Amr ibn Salih and Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smelled garlic and said: ""Who is this?"" He said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah; I adjure you, O Messenger of Allah - or: I have sworn upon you, O Messenger of Allah - that you put your hand in; and there was a band on his chest. He said: ""I see you have an excuse."""
"19186","1005 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Nasawi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Mahdi al-Missisi narrated to us, Umar ibn Rudayh narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Abu Burdah, from al-Mughirah, he said: The last campaign we fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he commanded us to wipe over our leather socks: ""For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night, so long as he does not remove them."""
"19187","Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami from al-Mughirah. 1006 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, they said: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, they said: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abd al-Mu'min, from Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, wiped over his leather socks, prayed, and placed me at his right."
"19188","Qabisah ibn Burmah al-Asadi from al-Mughirah. 1007 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, (H) and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Qabisah ibn Burmah al-Asadi, from al-Mughirah, he said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and we traveled until at the time of dawn he went off to a side, hid from me, then came, called for water for purification while wearing a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves; he brought his hand out from below the cloak, washed his face and hands, and wiped over his leather socks."
"19189","Suwayd ibn Sarhan from al-Mughirah. 1008 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, (H) and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, (H) and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, from Suwayd ibn Sarhan, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate food, the prayer was established, so he stood - and he had performed ablution before that - so I brought him water to perform ablution and he scolded me. That grieved me, by Allah, so I complained to Umar, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah was hurt by your scolding him and fears there is something in your heart against him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is nothing in my heart against him but good; rather he brought me water to perform ablution, though I had only eaten food - had I done so, the people after me would have done it."""
"19190","Ziyad ibn Ilaqah from al-Mughirah. 1009 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, he said: I heard Ziyad ibn Ilaqah saying: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah saying: He - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - would pray until his foot or his legs swelled, and it would be said to him, and he would say: ""Shall I not be a grateful servant?"""
"19191","1010 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray until his feet cracked, and it was said to him: Has Allah not forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? He said: ""Shall I not be a grateful servant?"""
"19192","1011 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray until his feet swelled, and it was said to him concerning that: Do you do this when Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? He said: ""Shall I not be a grateful servant?"""
"19193","1012 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us, they said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer."""
"19194","1013 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the dead, lest you harm the living."""
"19195","1014 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, (H) and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, they said: Za'idah narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah saying: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they are not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life. When you see them, supplicate to Allah and pray until it clears."""
"19196","1015 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Isra'il informed me, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they are not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life. When you see them, devote yourselves to supplication until it clears."""
"19197","1016 - Mahmud ibn Ali al-Bazzaz al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Awanah and Qays and Shayban narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, the sun eclipsed, and the people said: It eclipsed for the death of Ibrahim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: ""O people, the sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life; rather they are two signs among the signs of Allah. When that happens, pray until it clears."""
"19198","1017 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Kufi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is none but that a companion from the jinn has been assigned to him."" They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Not even I, except that Allah aided me against him and he submitted, so he commands me only with good."""
"19199","1018 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Talhah al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"19200","1019 - Mahmud ibn Ali al-Bazzar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah prayed and stood up in the first two rak'ahs; they glorified Allah to alert him and he continued in his prayer. When he finished he prostrated twice, and said: Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
